{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help","id":988329,"title":"New Gm needs some help.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-16T12:07:06-07:00","id":988329,"title":"New Gm needs some help.","content":"Hi guys, as per topic <br /> <br /> I have a group of 4 maybe 5 people who want to play mage. I have some experience with WOD, was a gm for vampire, played old mage for a while so I'm open to the idea. <br /> However I had a few questions if that's ok :<br /> <br /> 1) two players have a tendency for power gaming, is there anything in particular that i should watch out ? To nip it in the bud so to speak.<br /> <br /> 2) Would you have any advice for a new game, and this system? General info of what to do and what to avoid? etc.<br /> <br /> 3) Finally, should I start with the awakening as preludium? And if so, should it be done solo or as part of the main game?<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T12:33:46-07:00","id":988335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help#post988329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) two players have a tendency for power gaming, is there anything in particular that i should watch out ? To nip it in the bud so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay! This is a big one.<br /> Mage's Magick system is incredibly flexible, and incredibly potent. With all the spheres and all their levels combined, there is next to nothing that isn't possible.<br /> So something you *will* run into, given that you are not experienced with the system yet, is that something that seemed like a good idea at first, rule-wise, regarding a specific type of Magick or effect...becomes Bad Stuff once your players learn how to blow it out of proportion.<br /> <br /> So both you *and* your players need to be in agreement, that there will be events of 'Yes, I know I allowed that a few games ago, but I now see how that rule is bad at this level. I'm learning'. You as a new Mage GM need that flexibility, and they need to give it to you.<br /> <br /> I also highly encourage you to ask questions here regarding certain kinds of Magick, effects, rules etc. once your game starts. Or heck, even before. Lots of threads to read, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Would you have any advice for a new game, and this system? General info of what to do and what to avoid? etc. </div> </div> </div>An important thing to drive home to the players, and for you as a GM to remember, set-up and use is... that Mages are normal humans. If they are not working magick, they are plain, normal humans. They have friends, family, they need money, get tired, hungry, and whatever else comes with the human condition. They don't soak Lethal or Agg, without use of Magick they have mortal healing times...<br /> <br /> Watch out for you or your players treating a Mage (at first at least) as something non-human like a Vampire or Werewolf. The vast majority of Mages grew up as normal humans, still have human ties and interests. Just because you can do Magick doesn't mean you suddenly turn into ice-cold-combat-beast that is-not-shaken-by-anything either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ..and balancing a normal life and magick studies can be...interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Finally, should I start with the awakening as preludium? And if so, should it be done solo or as part of the main game? </div> </div> </div>If there is no encounter planned pretty much immediately on awakening with the other players, solo it. If you are playing Orphans, then you could do two awakenings solo, have those two players meet in a session, have the third player awaken solo, meet the other two til the group has met.<br /> <br /> If they are part of the Traditions or Technocracy, it's usually good to have the players meet after they have been in the faction for a while, or at least all have been introduced into their faction already, so it's all solo awakening sessions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, if a player already has Mage experience and knows how to describe awakenings and what they include, they simply can make the awakening part of their background writeup if they are willing to come up with it. That gives them the chance to let them develop their own nuances and events of the awakening, the people involved etc., and you don't need to do a solo session with that player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T12:45:19-07:00","id":988343,"title":"","content":"Ummm.... firstly this is the Forum for oWoD Mage.<br /> <br /> As for your actual questions... Mind you this is from a point of view of Revised. Others here have more (read: Any) Experience with M20.<br /> <br /> 1.) EVERYTHING. The entire system is designed in such a way that if you look for it, there are things to smash the world over your knee with.<br /> <br /> 1.A.) Paradox. By default, Paradox in revised maxes out at 12 for a botched vulgar effect of sphere 5. The reason for this is because, as I understand it, the ST is meant to ad-hoc paradox appropriate to the effect.<br /> <br /> 1.B.) Ritual Magic can get silly. If you let your players sit in their sanctum and perform a ritual almost ANY sphere can cause mass devastation. It has a potential to backfire of course, but you can get things like the Charles Atlas Training camp. Or the Holy Blade of Death where they've stacked umpteen bajillion successes into a relatively low sphere effect to get devastating results.<br /> <br /> 1.C.) Crafting requires more investment than the above, but depending on the version used can get completely silly.<br /> <br /> 2.) Personally, I'd say don't treat this like you would Vampire. The very nature of the system defies a lot of attempts to keep the game on rails. Correspondence allowing teleportation, Being able to see through Time, and so on. The sheer wealth of Options Mage gives means you'd be hard pressed to keep up with them all. So instead I'd advise keeping a living city. Have your foes be less &quot;One big bad guy who personally does everything.&quot; and instead have them operate through proxies and such. Encourage scuffles over territory with other mages to distract from the main foe. In general, don't allow them to just find the bad guy and kill the bad guy.<br /> <br /> 3.) Depends on what you want. Personally, Every game I've played has started after the players were already awakened and somewhat established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 10-16-2016, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T13:06:28-07:00","id":988350,"title":"","content":"Regarding 1+2:<br /> Start small. If possible go for apprentice level.<br /> Which leads to 3:<br /> Let them awake together in the first session.<br /> Alternatively solo awakenings.<br /> <br /> A cabal of Orphans with Arete at 1 is much more manageable than a group with 2 Arete 3 mages and 2 not so optimized mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T13:28:13-07:00","id":988363,"title":"","content":"Great answers guys, really appreciate it all. I bought this: Mage the ascension 20th anniversary edition. I assumed it's oWOD, am I mistaken? Would you recommend I run different version of mage at this stage?<br /> <br /> Also, given my experience with previous mage games - how far should I go into planning a chronicle? I know mage is prone to have things get out of hand with magic vaporizing most of the plot, therefore should I just focus on the main idea and go with the flow? <br /> <br /> Last question ( I think! ), would you have any ideas how to encourage my group to like this system? I came up with certain scenes where I adres their backgrounds, merits and flaws to show how deep this system can get but maybe there is more to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T13:36:33-07:00","id":988368,"title":"","content":"Nah, M20 is quite fine, and it's oWoD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T13:52:07-07:00","id":988374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=988363#post988363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, given my experience with previous mage games - how far should I go into planning a chronicle? I know mage is prone to have things get out of hand with magic vaporizing most of the plot, therefore should I just focus on the main idea and go with the flow?</div> </div> </div> </div>My advice would be to build their opposition. Then once you know what they want, and what they can do, build a plot from there. Same with their theoretical 'neighbors' I STRONGLY advise reading Pact's first few chapters because it gives a good look into newly awakened magery storywise, though that's not the intention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://pactwebserial.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://s0.wp.com/i/blank.jpg?m=1383295312i\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pactwebserial.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> Pact </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pactwebserial.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://pactwebserial.wordpress.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Devils and Details </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T13:55:39-07:00","id":988376,"title":"","content":"I will check it out now cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:25:22-07:00","id":988397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=988350#post988350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cabal of Orphans with Arete at 1 is much more manageable than a group with 2 Arete 3 mages and 2 not so optimized mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be very careful with this, because new players tend to react very poorly to having to start with Arete 1.<br /> <br /> Arete 1 allows very few effects that feel like you're really &quot;doing magic.&quot; Since it caps you at 1 dot in your Spheres, almost all your magic is based on perceptions rather than &quot;doing&quot; things.<br /> <br /> It also makes it very hard to get used to the Ascension magic system because - again - there's such a big limit on what you can do that you don't explore the flexibility in the system.<br /> <br /> There's also the XP issue. Buying Arete 2 and your first Sphere to 2 is a ton of XP, so it will take a long time to get to the point where the players feel like magic can actually do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:53:51-07:00","id":988423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=988363#post988363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great answers guys, really appreciate it all. I bought this: Mage the ascension 20th anniversary edition. I assumed it's oWOD, am I mistaken? Would you recommend I run different version of mage at this stage?<br /> <br /> Also, given my experience with previous mage games - how far should I go into planning a chronicle? I know mage is prone to have things get out of hand with magic vaporizing most of the plot, therefore should I just focus on the main idea and go with the flow?<br /> <br /> Last question ( I think! ), would you have any ideas how to encourage my group to like this system? I came up with certain scenes where I adres their backgrounds, merits and flaws to show how deep this system can get but maybe there is more to it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mage 20th Anniversary Edition, (Or M20 as we call it) is indeed part of oWOD. If it's got the Technocracy in it, it's old world. If you think you can handle the girth of this tome, then by all means go with it. If you're struggling to get through it, though, Revised can offer your a smaller amount of stuff to read (though the rules are somewhat different for combat, paradox, and some spheres), also this book is very much a product of its time, and M20 offers up a number of useful updates, making mage fit in with 2013 trappings. Some people really like 2nd Ed, but I'm not a huge fan of that book personally.<br /> <br /> When it comes to planning a chronicle, it's always a personal and subjective thing. Some people need whole books filled with plans to feel confident with their game, others literally right up a few notes the night before. It's all up to what you feel like you need. That being said, be prepared for the players to ignore a huge amount of what you've set up, and get ready to embrace whatever plans and wishes they throw in. I tend to keep things pretty fast and loose. The extent of my planning is Characters and Events. If there's a particular encounter I want to happen, I'll keep a lot of details vague until the time comes to throw it in, then I'll use the context of the scene to fill in the gaps on the fly.<br /> The biggest headache you can create for yourself is preparing too much and getting yourself stuck in a narrative corner. If there is this one shiny thing that the Players must have or the game falls apart, then they have to get it. If they miss it just because of a bad Perception roll, then you're going to have problems.<br /> <br /> The best advice I can give regarding plot is &quot;Consequences are your friend&quot;. Nothing your players do should go unpunished. If they kill something, someone is going to make them answer to it, be it via tribunal, police, or revenge. If they piss of a demon, the demon's coming after them. If they anger a Chantry leader, it's unlikely they'll get far with negotiations. Paradox is the ultimate consequence for abusing magic, and never be afraid to throw in an extra point or two if they do something particularly outlandish.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, if you want to encourage new people into the system, you need to let them feel just how powerful the spheres can be. Give special attention to their Avatar and personalise the way their avatar might communicate with them based on the Essence they choose. Be sure to go deep into Paradigm, encourage them to personalise how they do magic. This means working with each player individually on how they think magic works and what they believe they are doing to reality when they are making changes, and encourage your mages to have in character debates/arguments about what actually is happening when magic is being done. These kind of conversations are what Mage is all about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:21:55-07:00","id":988442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=988423#post988423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my opinion, if you want to encourage new people into the system, you need to let them feel just how powerful the spheres can be. Give special attention to their Avatar and personalise the way their avatar might communicate with them based on the Essence they choose. Be sure to go deep into Paradigm, encourage them to personalise how they do magic. This means working with each player individually on how they think magic works and what they believe they are doing to reality when they are making changes, and encourage your mages to have in character debates/arguments about what actually is happening when magic is being done. These kind of conversations are what Mage is all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this man, sounds very cool. I must say the concept of Paradigm sounds absolutely new to me! I don't think that was in the first mage I used to play. I will have to read properly about this and much more obviously. As to the chronicle, I have a general idea that I shamefully stole from the terrible warriors podcast. As a tryout and test, the group is asked to retrieve an item that is being auctioned very soon. They have a timeframe, objective and let's say motivation ( Status in the mage world I presume, I have to work on this as most of my players are very pissy about being forced to do something ). How they do this is up to them as I plan to give one rule 'don't screw this up'. Item is some valuable thing to the mentors etc. So this way I think they can be quite creative with HOW they get it - steal, buy, rob, leave it and do something else etc. I have a few complications in my mind to throw at them while at it ( different item in the said auction is a relic desired by some Tremere, chances are the group will get it as well and I will pick it up from there). Throw an agent of Technocracy as an observer, and a few more. <br /> <br /> One thing that keeps me thinking is how do I present traditions. I plan to run this game in NY, US. Not sure how to build up the mage ladder there yet, but I'm getting there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:25:59-07:00","id":988448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help#post988329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys, as per topic<br /> <br /> I have a group of 4 maybe 5 people who want to play mage. I have some experience with WOD, was a gm for vampire, played old mage for a while so I'm open to the idea.<br /> However I had a few questions if that's ok :<br /> <br /> 1) two players have a tendency for power gaming, is there anything in particular that i should watch out ? To nip it in the bud so to speak.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The answer to dealing with potential rule abuse and power gaming is always to talk to the player, not to limit his or her character. That only makes them miserable and encourages them to game the system in another way and boy, can Mage be gamed. The player is where the problem lies, deal with the root problem instead of trying to impose limitations. Can you guys establish why they feel the need to power game and deal with that? Fine. If not, then nothing's going to change.<br /> <br /> A lot of players feel they need to power game because they've played with unfair STss who took pride in sticking PCs in unfair situations and then killing them off. Thus, they feel the need to be able to protect themselves from the ST at all times. It is vital, especially in Storyteller games, to make sure everybody understands that players and STs are not enemies, they're allies and working together to create a story. Make sure they feel that they are able to trust you. Sure, PC death can (and indeed sometimes should) happen. But as long as the players know it won't come from the old &quot;well, you failed your alertness (diff 9) while sleeping, so now you're dead&quot; they'll be able to relax and go more with the flow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Then, of course, there are douchebags and you can't do anything about douchebags.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4259-eddie-fiori","name":"Eddie Fiori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:49:32-07:00","id":988473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=988442#post988442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like this man, sounds very cool. I must say the concept of Paradigm sounds absolutely new to me! I don't think that was in the first mage I used to play. I will have to read properly about this and much more obviously. As to the chronicle, I have a general idea that I shamefully stole from the terrible warriors podcast. As a tryout and test, the group is asked to retrieve an item that is being auctioned very soon. They have a timeframe, objective and let's say motivation ( Status in the mage world I presume, I have to work on this as most of my players are very pissy about being forced to do something ). How they do this is up to them as I plan to give one rule 'don't screw this up'. Item is some valuable thing to the mentors etc. So this way I think they can be quite creative with HOW they get it - steal, buy, rob, leave it and do something else etc. I have a few complications in my mind to throw at them while at it ( different item in the said auction is a relic desired by some Tremere, chances are the group will get it as well and I will pick it up from there). Throw an agent of Technocracy as an observer, and a few more.<br /> <br /> One thing that keeps me thinking is how do I present traditions. I plan to run this game in NY, US. Not sure how to build up the mage ladder there yet, but I'm getting there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a good framework for a game. Everyone's player group is different, so only you will know what your group needs. Only thing I'd suggest is if your players start to do something completely else or subvert the plot entirely, just go with it. Perhaps they disregard their mentors, does that mean their mentors are going to &quot;teach&quot; them something about respect? Also, as long as the story is interesting and the players are enjoying it, the game is a success.<br /> <br /> The traditions can be done however you want to do them. You can make Tradition politics as big or as little a part of your game as you'd prefer. Perhaps the traditions are breathing down the necks of your players, or maybe they've got better things to deal with than a bunch of misfit apprentices.<br /> Regardless of how involved they are, I'd offer the following advice for reading up on these guys. Read generally about everyone, read specifically only about the relevant ones. What's relevant will depend on what you want to put into your game, but your player's chosen tradition will certainly get priority.<br /> <br /> As for setting it in NY, it's so diverse that arguably any of the traditions would have a base of operations there. Ecstatics at the clubs, Verbena selling herbs in the Health store, Akashiks teaching Judo to teens, Hermetics making diagrams of the stock market, Dreamspeakers leading sermons on spirituality. You can place them wherever you need to and have them doing whatever makes sense and benefits the story.<br /> <br /> Mages are humans, and all humans have different ideas on how traditional teachings may be interpreted. Just as there may be Dreamspeakers that embrace technology for their shamanistic rituals, there may be Etherites that look at modern day technology, and condemn it for its lack of steam pipes and clockwork gears. The traditions are a collection of stereotypes and archetypes, but the individual mages within them can choose how much they adhere to or reject the teachings of the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:51:28-07:00","id":988664,"title":"","content":"Even if you end up using the Revised guide over M20 (M20 is, after all, a brick of a tome), you absolutely should at least read the chapter on Focus (what M20 calls Paradigm). It explains how Mages view their magick better than anything else Mage: The Ascension ever published on the subject. It divides things neatly into three categories - Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments - and gives a wealth of examples for each, for a very wide selection to choose from.<br /> <br /> If you can, get your players to read this chapter as well, though you might need to copy/paste the text if they don't have their own copies. It's worth the effort, though, as it gets them thinking about not just what they want to do (the Spheres), but how they want to do it. It's all very flexible, too, letting you pick, choose, and mix options in theoretically infinite ways. This is because all Mages have at least 7 Instruments, and can have anywhere from one to three Practices. Once you get them thinking about how Practices can meld together, their imaginations will run wild.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Once you do that, and the game starts, make sure to talk to them about how their chosen Focus affects their options. Because of course, while the Spheres are broad, how a character thinks they can use those Spheres can be significantly more limited. For example: from a scientific standpoint (Paradigm), Darkness is merely the absence of Light. But from a more mystical or fringe science worldview, Darkness is a force unto itself, in polar opposition to Light. This distinction can be very important to a Mage, as it makes the difference between being able to use Forces to manipulate Darkness directly, or if they can only manipulate indirectly by manipulating Light.<br /> <br /> Or, you have the difference between Germ Theory and Miasma Theory of disease. A Miasmatist - because they have an explanation for why disease happens - can still manipulate illness with Life. But since their scientific model doesn't incorporate micro-organisms, even if they buy the modern conception of Germ Theory (most Mages born in the modern day are familiar with Consensus Science, even if their methods deviate wildly from it), they don't have tools capable of interacting with germs directly. Same with a witch or shaman, who says that diseases are caused by spirits. They have no traditional methods for interacting with bacteria and viruses, and so can't work with them isolated from their effects on the body.<br /> <br /> Between mystic groups, there are differences in world view that make certain Instruments not an option. An Akashic, for instance, can't use True Names, because they might not believe True Names have any power (they don't even believe there is such a thing as a Self, separate from one's environment). A Hermetic, though, can use True Names, but won't get anywhere trying to perform Effects by denying their Ego (as a Hermetic's conception of Self and Will are integral to their ability to do magic).<br /> <br /> These are just to fringe cases. One's Focus is built on an internally consistent system for why the world works (Paradigm), and how one can exploit that system (Practice). Combine this with the fact that the Spheres are broad enough that it's hard for any one Mage to understand all its principles (read: Specialties). So a player Mage is going to be limited - at least out of the gate - in how they can use the Spheres. This is not an insurmountable problem, however, if the player character is willing to put in effort. Either by studying what members of their own Tradition have already learned on a subject, or by devising a theory that circumvents Paradigmatic limitations.<br /> <br /> How does a Hermetic, for instance, manipulate Radiation? That's a good question, and one worth exploring with further study. If the Hermetic is diligent, creative, and lucky, they could devise a theory within the Hermetic Paradigm that allows for them to act on Radiation in much the same way they act on wind or fire. (For the record, Radiation has been a known quantity in Science for a while, and therefore has been studied heavily by Hermetics. As such, this is one where study and information trading comes into play, assuming the character doesn't want to go to unnecessary effort).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T00:01:37-07:00","id":988720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=988397#post988397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be very careful with this, because new players tend to react very poorly to having to start with Arete 1.<br /> <br /> Arete 1 allows very few effects that feel like you're really &amp;quot;doing magic.&amp;quot; Since it caps you at 1 dot in your Spheres, almost all your magic is based on perceptions rather than &amp;quot;doing&amp;quot; things.<br /> <br /> It also makes it very hard to get used to the Ascension magic system because - again - there's such a big limit on what you can do that you don't explore the flexibility in the system.<br /> <br /> There's also the XP issue. Buying Arete 2 and your first Sphere to 2 is a ton of XP, so it will take a long time to get to the point where the players feel like magic can actually do anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the players are uncomfortable with it, you can tell them to withhold points at chargen. As soon as you and your players get more comfortable with m20 you can issue some or all of the points.<br /> Or you go for full chargen and tell a realky long preludium.<br /> Or you gift them points directly.<br /> <br /> Or...<br /> All methods tend to produce more balanced and detailed chars IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T01:14:13-07:00","id":988732,"title":"","content":"The problem is that you can't really learn the M20 rules with Arete 1, because you never really get into most of the magic variations until 2 or 3. All you're going to learn is the core WoD rules, that the OP is already used to from running VtM.<br /> <br /> I don't think you're wrong in that Mage works well if a lot of time spent on backstory, however you want to get to it, but it's really hard to know what to do with a backstory without either (a) an experienced Mage player/ST to help out, or (b) playing the game a bit without it to see what you're missing.<br /> <br /> Sure, this is just my personal experience, but I have never seen anyone really enjoy Mage playing an Arete 1 character unless they'd already played a character with Arete 2-3 at start first. I have seen at least a dozen players say, &quot;Oh, I'll just start with Arete 1 to ease into things so I can learn as I go,&quot; and it has never worked out because they all run into the same problem of never actually learning the system without enough Arete and Sphere levels to play with the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T01:31:58-07:00","id":988736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=988732#post988732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, this is just my personal experience, but I have never seen anyone really enjoy Mage playing an Arete 1 character unless they'd already played a character with Arete 2-3 at start first. I have seen at least a dozen players say, &quot;Oh, I'll just start with Arete 1 to ease into things so I can learn as I go,&quot; and it has never worked out because they all run into the same problem of never actually learning the system without enough Arete and Sphere levels to play with the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's for this reason that I'd advocate giving players a free dot of Arete to start with. Most people who decide to play Mage desire to actually do magick. It's the point of the system, and forcing them to spend some of their character creation points just to do so is kind of a dick move.<br /> <br /> If any players, for whatever reason, want to start at Arete 1, you can always buy it back for freebie points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T03:44:09-07:00","id":988770,"title":"","content":"A possible solution (maintaining Arete 1) is to give out Wonders with Arete 3 effects. This way you have magick that is not as surprising and storysmashing as usual.<br /> A group of apprentices going to town with their masters toys...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T03:50:32-07:00","id":988772,"title":"","content":"The other thing you could do is wave the Ar\u00eate Exp cost and just give the players a seeking when it feels correct narratively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:12:54-07:00","id":988821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help#post988329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys, as per topic<br /> <br /> I have a group of 4 maybe 5 people who want to play mage. I have some experience with WOD, was a gm for vampire, played old mage for a while so I'm open to the idea.<br /> However I had a few questions if that's ok :<br /> <br /> 1) two players have a tendency for power gaming, is there anything in particular that i should watch out ? To nip it in the bud so to speak.<br /> <br /> 2) Would you have any advice for a new game, and this system? General info of what to do and what to avoid? etc.<br /> <br /> 3) Finally, should I start with the awakening as preludium? And if so, should it be done solo or as part of the main game?<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with much of what has already been suggested starting at Arete 2, allowing takebacks on rulings, reading the Focus section.<br /> <br /> If you are using the M20 through PDF format I would print out the Combat System Charts (pgs 445 - 457) and the Casting Magickal Effects and Magickal Reference Charts (501 - 510). Both of those are immensely useful to have on hand, especially the Magickal charts considering the complexity and open-ended nature of True Magic (aka Awakened Magic, Magick).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One thing that keeps me thinking is how do I present traditions. I plan to run this game in NY, US. Not sure how to build up the mage ladder there yet, but I'm getting there. </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Dont worry about having stats for the mages of the region, rather just a descriptor of their relative level of mystical power Initiate (Arete 1-2) Adept (Arete 3-4) Master (Arete 5+) and their affiliation and sect.</li> <li>Worry more about presenting the traditions the characters follow than the others. Also unlike in a game like Vampire, there is not a central authority like a Prince among the Mages of a city. Rather a city (especially larger ones) may be home to one or more chantries and there may be multiple masters and cabals within those.</li> <li>Traditions are not straitjackets, but rather groups of similarly minded and trained Mages. This means two mages of the same Tradition while being similar might still have many differences.</li> <li>Dont think about a ladder in terms of a region, but rather a chantry. Figure out which mages hold authority within a chantry and why. Then think about what area/node(s) that chantry has influence over and whether they have had contact with any of the other mages/chantries in the area. If so what kind of contact, do they know about each other but not much else, do they have dealings with each other (trading services, training, etc), do they interact peacefully or are they in conflict. Larger chantries with more members and holdings are generally going to have more influence than smaller ones. If a small chantry does have a lot of 'pull' why? Does it have more powerful mages, are its members wealthier or more connected than others, do they have access to a powerful node, etc?</li> <li>Remember Mages are still in many ways normal humans, and until one reaches the echelons of the masters, they are going to need the contact and interactions with normal society. So think about how they do that, do they have family in the region, what sort of influence(s) do they have, what properties do they own? An Etherite with ties to high finance and regularly attends stockholder/board meetings is going to come off differently than another Etherite who volunteers at the local library and offers tutoring to college students; remember this when presenting them, Traditions are made up of individuals not faceless legions.</li> <li>What sort of connection do mages of the same Tradition have within the region. Figure out how likely it is for a mage of a particular Tradition to know another member. If they do know of other members, do they have their own separate hierarchy (Hermetics are especially likely to have this).</li> <li>Determine what sorts of interactions the chantries have with other mages in the region. Which mages/chantries does the Technocracy have knowledge of and how much? If there are Disparates do they have any interaction with either the Tradition mages or Technocratic agents?</li> <li>If there are any powerful spirits you want to have in the region, have they had any dealings with the mages of the area and if so how.</li> <li>If you are going to have any crossover (warning: if you are going to cross over make sure you are very familiar with the game you are crossing over with, Mage is hard enough dont overwhelm yourself) figure out how much the different supernaturals know of each other. Also what interactions if any do they have with the Mages of the region are they in conflict or have the interactions been peaceful.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> In terms of the initial questions.<br /> <br /> 1) As mentioned before, but worth repeating given appropriate Spheres and Arete nearly anything is possible with Awakened Magic and a power gamer can quickly figure out how to do very powerful things with even only a few Spheres.<br /> <br /> 2) See below<br /> <br /> 3) Either way is fine, depends on available time and player/ST preferences.<br /> <br /> Question 2 is broad so here is a whole pile of tips, hints, and advice for a new Mage ST/Player (in no particular order)<br /> <br /> Read through all the Spheres carefully at least twice. Knowing what the different Sphere levels can do makes figuring out Spheres needed for Magickal effects much easier.<br /> <br /> After character creation go through each character and have the group come up with a Magickal effect using the character's Spheres. This will give you all a chance to get familiar with building effects, assigning vulgarity, and seeing what difficulty reductions might be usable. Then have the player of that character try to describe how their character casts the effect within the Focus (Paradigm, Practices, and Instuments) of their Mage.<br /> <br /> Mages are normal humans in terms of soaking damage, so combat can be very lethal. Be aware of this and dont be afraid to pull punches if you suddenly feel like the threat you've put them against is suddenly a lot worse than you originally intended (basically takebacks).<br /> <br /> Read the Focus section. Thinking about and describing a Mage's magick through their focus is not only great for roleplay but can give you a better feel for how the character thinks.<br /> <br /> The characters' Avatars are an easy way to guide the characters and offer advice or hints. Don't overuse it, but it can be a helpful for when a player/the group is lost and just needs a hand.<br /> <br /> When designing a chantry and placing NPC mages, think about how those mages came to the chantry and why they remained. Think about how their Traditions and Focuses interact and shape the chantry, both physically and metaphysically.<br /> <br /> I have a pseudo-house rule that I call &quot;Are you sure?&quot; Whenever I add a new player to a group I tell them that if I ever stop, look them in the eye, and slowly ask &quot;Are you sure?&quot; It means that they are about to do something monumentally foolish, and should they continue I absolve myself regarding the consequences of their actions. There will be no pulled punches, no fudged dice rolls, no takebacks, no NPC to the rescue, if the character dies so be it roll up a new one. This doesnt mean I do this whenever the player is going to do something risky, foolish, or dangerous, but rather something so stupid and boneheaded that I can see no outcome other than their death(s) or the destruction of the game and they should immediately rethink their choice of action. Its a nebulous thing and I've only had to use it a couple of times over the 16 years I've been running games, when I have used it the player being jarred out of their thoughts for a moment was able to see the folly in their chosen path. I see it as a 'please dont ruin this chronicle/campaign/game just because you are being monumentally stupid'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:33:20-07:00","id":988828,"title":"","content":"My suggestion for power gamer is to send them to a paradox realm (they don't notice it until they start to supect) where they are witness of a confrotation between Superman and Son Goku (yes, to cause faces of WTF). Then when they start to suffer &quot;collateral damages&quot; they should learn power without wisdom is like a powerful car with bad control). Use the sense of humor with the paradox effects to hummilliate proud characters. <br /> <br /> Play with ambiguity, is that annoying character a Mary sue/Gary Stu, an allucination or a paradox spirit? Also you can use (Dreamwork's) minions (mmmmm, curious paradox effect) to teach an important lesson for real warriors. You can do a fight maneuver rightly thousands of times, but only once you fail and then you will be dead. <br /> <br /> Force them to be cautious. Corax or wereravens are like Gaia's journalist. A talking crow can be very annoying, and you can't kill anything is only an smoking illusory clone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T07:04:16-07:00","id":988844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=988772#post988772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing you could do is wave the Ar\u00eate Exp cost and just give the players a seeking when it feels correct narratively.</div> </div> </div> </div>That also serves another purpose: you don't feel compelled to make seekings easy because they paid for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T08:25:04-07:00","id":988869,"title":"","content":"And, speaking of seekings -<br /> <br /> Coming up and running seekings appropriate for the character, making then easy or challenging enough to reflect the appropriate level of Arete, and finding the right moment in a character's life for a seeking is probably *the* hardest things to get done right when you are a Mage GM.<br /> <br /> Both you and the player needs to be invested in the character's development, and you also should take notes - when the character makes good or bad experiences, has rivals, enemies or friends. What people, events and items affect them, or which ones they ignore when they shouldn't. How their paradigm hinders them at times, or brings them great success.<br /> <br /> And then challenge the character in the form of a metaphysical journey or puzzle. It needn't be a mindscape the character steps into durign dreamtime, but that's how most modern seekings happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T09:21:11-07:00","id":988890,"title":"","content":"My God, there is a lot of stuff that I need to prepare prior to running this game haha, appreciate all the help ! Keep it coming :-) I'm trying to update my print list for rulls/etc as I sadly don't have access to the GM screen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:28:44-07:00","id":988948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=988890#post988890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My God, there is a lot of stuff that I need to prepare prior to running this game haha, appreciate all the help ! Keep it coming :-) I'm trying to update my print list for rulls/etc as I sadly don't have access to the GM screen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is no GM screen for M20 just yet. It's in the works but it's not yet published.<br /> <br /> The important tables to get are the Combat table page and the Magic table page. Everything else is down to preference. For example, I love having the &quot;how long does damage take to heal&quot; chart as well as the Experience Cost chart on hand, because those are things that come up quite often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T07:04:16-07:00","id":989857,"title":"","content":"On the phone so not quoting.<br /> Waving xp cost for Arete is how I run my game. It alows me full control over sphere advancement. And the diference between sphere levels of 3 and 4 is huge. Also, especially for your first time, capping sphere level at 2 at chargen is a good way to get your players creative in their effect as well as let them truely experience growth when advancing to level 3 without becoming overly powerful. I'd strongly recommend all players beging at Arete 3 though as botching is way to easy at 2 and since most effect will require at least 2 successes 3 Arete lets the players work their standard effects in 2 turns or less","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T07:42:49-07:00","id":989869,"title":"","content":"With Arete, I tend to do both. I have a 1 time XP cost for the new level of Arete. Once they buy it, they have bought the chance to go on a Seeking. I put them on a Seeking at an appropriate time once I've figured out a good puzzle for them, and if they succeed then they get the point. If they fail, then depending on the degree of failure they'll either get kicked out and have to wait until I give them the seeking again, or they may suffer penalties like loss of WP or a resonance change.<br /> However, the Seeking will happen again. How consistent it is and how harsh the penalties are will depend on the subject at hand and the Avatar's Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T11:23:58-07:00","id":990507,"title":"","content":"Something that I don't think that I've seen directly addressed (if maybe tangentially) about your powergamers: Paradigm/Focus needs to be enforced. I've seen plenty of people come to forums or the table wanting to build a character whose Paradigm roughly equates to &quot;I see the truth of reality, and thus make my will manifest.&quot; Players who know how the Sphere system works, and who understand the Consensus, understand what we call the &quot;Purple Paradigm,&quot; and sometimes will try to make that transfer into character knowledge. That's a big no no. <br /> <br /> Instruments (or foci, whatever term you're using) that are more or less &quot;I cast the magick with my mind&quot; should be highly discouraged, or at least regulated. Skipping all the stumbling blocks and restrictions that is inherent Paradigm/Focus removes an enormous amount of depth from the game and is a clear path to powergaming.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that things like telekinesis, telepathy, and other tele- words are out of bounds for mages. On the contrary, they're pretty proliferate in the Society of Ether, and it's been at least &quot;studied&quot; in the halls of the Technoccracy. However, one can't, or shouldn't, simply say &quot;I do it with my mind.&quot; Explain it. How do you do it with your mind? What principles are you using? Why can't other people do it? Do you use a point of Willpower to represent using mind power to do it? Do you concentrate on/through a crystal that has a specific resonating property that magnifies your brain power? Do you see where I'm going with this?<br /> <br /> Magick, inherently in the system, has a price, some manner of inconvenience standing between a mage and immediate, unrestrained access to her magick. Maybe it's a dance or a chant, a magick word or a specific thought form, a consumed point of Willpower or a raised difficulty (as per the rules for casting without instruments).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:48:52-07:00","id":990646,"title":"","content":"Some ideas to simplify things at the start:<br /> <br /> Be clear with everyone that you are learning the rules along with them and may need to make decisions on the fly, and reserve the right to change your mind later.<br /> <br /> Sit down with the players and pick one tradition, and run as a single tradition. You simply do not have the time or energy to teach five different people five different paradigms, plus whatever npcs you need. Some people just don't grok technomagic or are turned off by the sex/drugs/rock and roll stuff. Find one everyone is comfortable with and can play. Avoid orphans, as newbies often need more defined boundaries than that. Hermetics, Verbena and, possibly, Hollow Ones can be good choices because they are so prominent in pop culture and other tabletop rpgs. You will only need to really understand that one paradigm in depth, and no one will get over-whelmed. Plus, the group will come out of the chronicle with a solid, solid understanding of at least one tradition. This will serve them well in later chronicles.<br /> <br /> Start with interesting characters as people, not mages. Make sure that all the characters have interesting and strong relationships with one another, whether friends or rivals. If they all have goals, fears, personal foibles and interesting back stories, just handing them some magick will lead to their producing a plot on their own. Just be ready to have the world around them react to their actions by having a good grasp of the characters and their environment. Maybe give them all a group mentor who initiates them into their Tradition to help move the plot forward, if necessary.<br /> <br /> Whatever else you do, start them weak.<br /> <br /> Begin first session with Arete 1 and three spheres at level one. The first play session will be learning the basic mechanics of the system, both magical and mundane. Make sure every player uses their magic at least once to try it out. That level of magic is more than enough to learn basic conjunctional effects and the concept of coincidentiality. Reward them with an additional dot of Arete and a second level in one sphere of their choice at the end of session one.<br /> <br /> This will give them an immediate sense of growth and power in session two, while still keeping things manageable. It will also let both you and them know which spheres you need to study up on. At the end of session two, give them all another level two dot, and an additional level one dot.<br /> <br /> This puts them at the book standard 5+1 sphere dots at the start of session three. Congratulations, the prelude is over! Use regular experience costs from there. Also, by now the plot should have advanced, on its own, to a point where it's self-sustaining. Someone will have used level one spheres to learn things about their families and co-workers they'd rather not know. Someone will have let power go to their head and deserve repercussions. Trust the process. The plot will happen if you let it. Just focus on believable characters and the mechanics for now.<br /> <br /> Good luck, and have fun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T23:41:52-07:00","id":990824,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11558_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11558\" data-vbnamecard=\"11558\">Nosimplehiway</a> you took the words right out of my mouth<br /> <br /> Such are the dangers of priorizing Mind over Expression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T04:54:19-07:00","id":991341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=990507#post990507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that I don't think that I've seen directly addressed (if maybe tangentially) about your powergamers: Paradigm/Focus needs to be enforced. I've seen plenty of people come to forums or the table wanting to build a character whose Paradigm roughly equates to &quot;I see the truth of reality, and thus make my will manifest.&quot; Players who know how the Sphere system works, and who understand the Consensus, understand what we call the &quot;Purple Paradigm,&quot; and sometimes will try to make that transfer into character knowledge. That's a big no no.<br /> <br /> Instruments (or foci, whatever term you're using) that are more or less &quot;I cast the magick with my mind&quot; should be highly discouraged, or at least regulated. Skipping all the stumbling blocks and restrictions that is inherent Paradigm/Focus removes an enormous amount of depth from the game and is a clear path to powergaming.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that things like telekinesis, telepathy, and other tele- words are out of bounds for mages. On the contrary, they're pretty proliferate in the Society of Ether, and it's been at least &quot;studied&quot; in the halls of the Technoccracy. However, one can't, or shouldn't, simply say &quot;I do it with my mind.&quot; Explain it. How do you do it with your mind? What principles are you using? Why can't other people do it? Do you use a point of Willpower to represent using mind power to do it? Do you concentrate on/through a crystal that has a specific resonating property that magnifies your brain power? Do you see where I'm going with this?<br /> <br /> Magick, inherently in the system, has a price, some manner of inconvenience standing between a mage and immediate, unrestrained access to her magick. Maybe it's a dance or a chant, a magick word or a specific thought form, a consumed point of Willpower or a raised difficulty (as per the rules for casting without instruments).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, your post and the previous ones that mentioned Paradigm ( Page 560 - 600 that I have read) did rise some questions yesterday at the character creation session we had. Basically:<br /> <br /> 1) Why do we have this limitation? I'm asking because I don't remember this from the first edition of mage. Also, since my players chose several different traditions ( and I'm ok with that ), they will have different paradigms - how does that work? I mean they will watch each other casting spells, dancing, using foci and all that - will that not change ones perspective if his way of doing magic is right? Does this whole paradigm not strike anyone more like a nuisance that fun addition to the game? <br /> <br /> 2) Second one that came up during the test of casting : The table for casting spells says 'highest ranking sphere+ something'. Does it mean that it gets harder to cast spells as players increase their sphere level? Or am I reading it wrong ?<br /> <br /> 3) Extended magic : is it just rolling and rolling and rolling until a player gets enough successes? Is there any drawback to this other that situational stuff where they're pressed to react now with no time for more rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T06:04:53-07:00","id":991360,"title":"","content":"1) Paradigm is arguably the central premise of Mage. The whole game is all about the idea that Belief shapes Reality, and that all conventions of Reality are simply the manifestation of shared practises and interpretations. In this way, anything magical can work if enough people belief it to work. The only reason Science works the way it does is because enough people believe in the Scientific Paradigm as popularised by the Technocracy. If, say, the Order of Heremes were in charge and most of humanity believed their consensus as truth, then Scientific instruments either would not work, or would highly vulgar magic.<br /> <br /> The reason this matters is because Mage is all about the hubris of paradaigm, and how every mage considers their view of reality to be the &quot;correct&quot; one, and that all others are either perverting reality, or are simply too caught up in their own world view to see things the &quot;right&quot; way. This is the main conflict between the Traditions and the Technocracy. From a completely subjective viewpoint, they are both doing the same thing, but neither one would ever admit that Enlightened Science and Traditional Magick are related.<br /> The Traditions consider the Technocracy to be suppressing their practices by enforcing their static view of reality on to sleepers, and thus may drive away humanities innate ability to shape the world around them.<br /> The Technocracy, on the other hand, would say that they are simply out to keep reality predictable enough to understand and control without need of awakening or specialist knowledge, and the Traditions are simply a group of close minded mystics who's &quot;arts&quot; are not only dangerous, but subvert the work of their own scientists in ensuring reality is predictable.<br /> <br /> So too is Paradigm important within the Traditions themselves. Each one comes from a different school of how magic is performed, and thus a different interpretation on what the Avatar is, on what Quintessence is, in what Nodes are, and what an act of magic requires in order to function.<br /> <br /> Verbena, for example, consider magic to be the very essence of life, and thus only by embracing natural things can one tune their mind to real magic. The Avatar is powerful spiritual force which guides you and Quintessence is that mystical life energy that flows through everything, and can be felt in blood.<br /> Akashics instead would say that all that is magic comes from within. The Avatar is a way of thinking about an internal power known as qi, one that can be harnessed with enough discipline and training, and quintessence is merely the manifestation of this Qi force.<br /> Etherites, however, would consider magic and science to be interchangeable, and that rather than doing something all mystic and old, what they're doing is taking advantage of long discarded theories to achieve amazing results. To them, the Avatar is more like Genius, a form of inspirational brilliance that few possess, while many have remarkably different theories on what Quintessence is and how to best utilise it.<br /> <br /> Even within a tradition, there are different prevailing paradigms. Order of Heremes for example:<br /> <br /> A lot of Hermetics believe that the words have intrinsic power in and of themselves, and the older the words, the more potent the power, whether that be the ancient tongues, or long dead scripture, these words hold within them secrets from a time when magic was as common as air, and as such invoking the power of these words brings about these powers.<br /> <br /> Another common theory amongst Hermetics is that the world is built upon language, that everything that we ever experience is simply built upon a foundation of thoughts and ideas, not unlike Plato's theory of the Forms. As such, if one can tap into the language of the universe, they can construct completely new sentences. In many ways this is not all that different from the Virtual Adepts belief of the Universal Source Code, but you'll never here a Hermetic admit this.<br /> There are a number of Hermetics that consider the very act of casting the spell to be the source of magic. It's not so much that the words have power, but that the act of saying these words puts your mind back in the same mindset of those in the past. So by saying the words, writing the runes, and enacting the rituals, you are able to replicate the effects done in years gone by. This idea is not unlike how Sorcerers perform magic, but applied to the Spheres. It has much more freedom than traditional Sorcery, but it's still highly ritualised.<br /> As one final example, there are Hermetics that consider Ancient Languages to be a direct method of communication with gods or angels, and so they use these methods of communication in order to attain a form of divine intervention. Depending on which belief the mage ascribes to, this could be to the ancient Egyptian gods, the Greek gods, or any of the other gods that make up the High Court of the Umbrood.<br /> <br /> All this serves that point that paradigm is as unique to the mage at the mage themselves, and the Traditions are little more than a way of grouping generally speaking like minded individuals and fostering the next generation with specific ideas to grow from. In many ways this is exactly what happens in the real world with culture.<br /> <br /> So what happens when a mage sees one who is doing magic unlike that which they perform? Depends on what they are looking at.<br /> <br /> A Hermetic from House Flambeau make look upon the charts and diagrams of a Hermetic from House Fortunae and have no idea what it is they are doing. While the former relies on Staves and Wands, the latter relies on Numbers and Charts. They recognise the importance and legitimacy of the other's work, but just simply don't have the expertise to understand what it is the other is doing. Sort of like when a Biologist and an Accountant try to teach one another of their trades. They don't instantly dismiss the other, but they don't quite understand what's going on either.<br /> <br /> This same House Flambeau Hermetic may look at the practices of the Akashic monks and recognise their solitary practice to achieve mental mastery is not unlike the Hermetic's own tradition which emphasises study, practice, and painstaking diligence to adhered methods. So while the methods may differ in places, they share a similar ethos of self actualisation. So he may conclude that, while he doesn't understand their methods, he can appreciate that it's all about Magic through hard work.<br /> If this Hermetic encountered a Verbena witch, on the other hand, their outlook on their practice would be much less favourable. Their magic is raw, uncivilised, and very messy, often times involving copious amounts of blood, sweat, and moonlight chanting. Their ways are outmoded, outdated, and firmly stuck in an ancient time that the Hermetics have long since developed from. The Verbena's magic is little more than sorcery as far as he's concerned. Sure they are capable of doing amazing things, but so are many other hedge mages. Their methods are simply barbaric and not to be encouraged.<br /> When faced with a Etherite, they may be curious by the toys that they produce, but at the end of the day that's all they are. At best they are a neat little distraction, and at worst they support the Technocratic paradigm and thus have a role in suppressing &quot;real&quot; magic. If an Etherite's tools have a basis in Hermetic mythology, however, they'd probably look more favourably upon them, though they would consider this scientist to be rather misguided in their approach.<br /> Faced with Hollow One, most Hermetics look down on them either in pity, or in anger. It takes years of dedicated study and practice for a Hermetic to achieve the level of power they have accrued, and these Goth kids are walking around firing off half-baked effects as if they were mere parlour tricks!? It's an absolute mockery. Get them out of my face!<br /> <br /> The fact that your players all chose different paradigms is actually a really good thing, it gives them a chance to roleplay these kinds of disputes. Perhaps a rivalry will spring up between two contrary factions, or maybe the similarities will be emphasised over the differences allowing the mages to work together. Philosophical discussions like these lie at the core of Mage, and I think they should always be encouraged when possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) It's not about how many dots in a sphere you have, it's about the highest sphere rate in the effect being cast. If your mage has Matter 3, then they can do Matter 1 effects, Matter 2 effects, and Matter 3 effects. Matter 1 effects, like determining what something is made off, will always be easier than a Matter 3 effect, like causing a wall to crumble into dust.<br /> <br /> 3) Extended magic, when not done as a Ritual, has the following drawbacks.<br /> <br /> - The difficulty of the magic increases by 1 for every extra roll (up to the limit of +3 base difficulty)<br /> - A Botch causes the entire thing to fall down, and in addition to the normal Botch paradox, you get an additional point per extra roll.<br /> - (optional) Any effect which gets above 10 successes is no longer coincidental, and thus gives the caster Paradox<br /> - (optional) If you want, you can set a failure limit. So if a mage fails more than the limit, then the effect fails completely.<br /> <br /> Making the extended magic roll a Ritual casting does the following<br /> <br /> - A lot of time is taken between rolls, depending on the complexity of the ritual this could be anywhere between 10 minutes to a whole hour per roll<br /> - Characters are therefor limited in terms of how much time they have as well as how much continuous work their body can take before collapsing.<br /> - The difficulty does not increase per roll<br /> - 10 successes does not turn a coincidental effect into a vulgar one.<br /> - Depending on what is being done, many more effects may be considered coincidental when cast in this way.<br /> - A Failure results in a single rise in difficulty<br /> - A Botch results in the entire effect botching, paradox is given out as stated above.<br /> - Will Power can be used to turn a Botch into a Failure, but only once per ritual, and this results in a single success being lost from the count.<br /> <br /> - Mages may work together on rituals. The requirements are that each mage must have the minimum Sphere Rank required to perform the spell on their own.<br /> - Mages working in tandem like this will roll individually and pool successes together. A single botch results in the entire effect botching and everyone getting paradox.<br /> - Mages who have at least one dot in all the spheres required, but lack the appropriate levels, may still contribute a single success to the pool.<br /> <br /> Extended rolls the quick way may work while in a battle, especially for things that only require 5 or 10 successes.<br /> But when you're trying to do something that requires 20, 40, or even 60 successes, doing this without a Ritual is pretty impossible. The risk of a botch becomes all too real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 10-22-2016, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:06:23-07:00","id":991472,"title":"","content":"Thank you Saikou :-) as always on point !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:06:06-07:00","id":991607,"title":"","content":"To expand on Saikou's point, understand that a Focus is not just a set of recipes or tricks. It's a World View, that the Mage must internalize in order to make use of. A Chorister truly <i>believes</i> in the power and primacy of her particular vision of God. An Ecstasy Cultist truly <i>believes</i> that the world around them is an illusion, malleable with but the right change in perception. The Son of Ether truly <i>believes</i> in the existence of the luminiferous ether, and the technological applications of same. These are deep-seated models for reality that Mages hold dear, important not only to their perceptions of the world, but to their self-identity. And it's a World View they've spent at least a few years training in, ever since they Awakened (if not before, in the case of religious persons or former Sorcerers). <br /> <br /> So when a Mage sees another Mage performing Magick in a manner contrary to the way they've been taught or learned for themselves, their beliefs won't crumble just like that. It can give them Cognitive Dissonance, yes, but human beings are exemplary at resolving Cognitive Dissonance. They can simply come up with any number of rationalizations for the contradiction. The Tradition Council (and the Traditions themselves, internally) are an alliance of convenience, built upon a web of such rationalizations, and a polite mutual agreement not to make a big deal about it.<br /> <br /> When you get back to your game, then, take the players aside for a moment and help them understand this fact. That even if the players understand that Focus is a construction, that their characters are fully and completely committed to the World Views that fuel their Magick. Even if they can understand another Mage's point of view, knowing it intellectually and internalizing it are two different things. Then, ask the players what their characters think of their fellow PCs, and what they think each other are doing from the lens of their own Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T04:35:19-07:00","id":991805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=991607#post991607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To expand on Saikou's point, understand that a Focus is not just a set of recipes or tricks. It's a World View, that the Mage must internalize in order to make use of. A Chorister truly <i>believes</i> in the power and primacy of her particular vision of God. An Ecstasy Cultist truly <i>believes</i> that the world around them is an illusion, malleable with but the right change in perception. The Son of Ether truly <i>believes</i> in the existence of the luminiferous ether, and the technological applications of same. These are deep-seated models for reality that Mages hold dear, important not only to their perceptions of the world, but to their self-identity. And it's a World View they've spent at least a few years training in, ever since they Awakened (if not before, in the case of religious persons or former Sorcerers).<br /> <br /> So when a Mage sees another Mage performing Magick in a manner contrary to the way they've been taught or learned for themselves, their beliefs won't crumble just like that. It can give them Cognitive Dissonance, yes, but human beings are exemplary at resolving Cognitive Dissonance. They can simply come up with any number of rationalizations for the contradiction. The Tradition Council (and the Traditions themselves, internally) are an alliance of convenience, built upon a web of such rationalizations, and a polite mutual agreement not to make a big deal about it.<br /> <br /> When you get back to your game, then, take the players aside for a moment and help them understand this fact. That even if the players understand that Focus is a construction, that their characters are fully and completely committed to the World Views that fuel their Magick. Even if they can understand another Mage's point of view, knowing it intellectually and internalizing it are two different things. Then, ask the players what their characters think of their fellow PCs, and what they think each other are doing from the lens of their own Focus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The only issue I have with said 'Cognitive Dissonance' in this case as opposed to said religion views in out modern society is that different paradigms actually work. IF a Verbena sees that a VA is successful in his magic with a tablet and math - why he or she would still maintain belief in witchcraft? In reference to Cognitive Dissonance among Muslim VS Christians, neither can proove their point and much is set in belief. In mage results happen almost instantly and there is actual proof? Not sure if I'm making this easy to understand :-/ sorry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T05:01:15-07:00","id":991807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=991805#post991805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> The only issue I have with said 'Cognitive Dissonance' in this case as opposed to said religion views in out modern society is that different paradigms actually work. IF a Verbena sees that a VA is successful in his magic with a tablet and math - why he or she would still maintain belief in witchcraft? In reference to Cognitive Dissonance among Muslim VS Christians, neither can proove their point and much is set in belief. In mage results happen almost instantly and there is actual proof? Not sure if I'm making this easy to understand :-/ sorry</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Verbena's magick still works, and to the Verbena's mind may work better than anything the Virtual Adept could do. Further, the Verbena may view the Virtual Adept's use of computers as being too divorced from life to be acceptable. It doesn't mean they'll necessarily try to force the VA to work magick like a Verbena, but it likely means they will not respect the VA's magick as much as their own.<br /> <br /> Why would someone who has their own <i>working</i> magick abandon it for the first different practice they come across? Just because it works? <i>Their own magick works</i>. This is often a source of friction and conflict, but doesn't typically lead to mages abandoning their paradigms for &quot;greener pastures.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T06:08:15-07:00","id":991815,"title":"","content":"If a verbena sees a VA hack a plant to grow, they'll be outraged. They are treating the mystic energy of life as cold and unfeeling numbers. There is no spirit, no compassion, the greatest thing on the planet has ren reduced to a machine.<br /> <br /> If a VA saw a verbena do life magic, they'll be amused. Cool little tricks you got there, bit dirty though. All that mud, sweat, blood. Not my thing. You do you tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T06:24:36-07:00","id":991821,"title":"","content":"There are many ways to deal with Cognitive Dissonance. One of these, yes, is to abandon one's original beliefs for new ones. But that only happens if the new evidence is too compelling to ignore. And humans have an enormous threshold for what counts as compelling enough to make them reject everything they've believed. Especially if they can think of something - anything - that can rationalize that evidence within the bounds of one's existing world view.<br /> <br /> It's significantly easier to come up with excuses, twist logic to suit one's ends, or simply reject the evidence out of hand (at which point, because of Confirmation Bias, they will unconsciously selectively forget evidence that contradicts their views, while remembering clearly evidence that supports them). I mean easier from a cognitive energy standpoint, as well as from the standpoint of simply avoiding having to confront the idea that their views may be wrong (a painful proposition, and one people dodge out of whenever possible).<br /> <br /> Plus, as Resplendent Fire said, the Mage's original world view <i>works</i>. It provides them a framework for performing miracles. This is, from the Mage's perspective, irrefutable evidence in support of their vision of reality. That someone else can perform different acts to accomplish the same things is not a deal-breaker in most Mage's eyes. Is this Hubris? Most certainly. But it's also completely understandable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:46:37-07:00","id":991902,"title":"","content":"This was addressed in Guide to the Traditions.<br /> Your Paradigm can be Rigid, Open Minded, Liberal etc. If you adhere strictly to your view and don't even give other views a sporting chance (difficult nowadays due to globalization) then you run into problems if an ally performs stuff that shouldn't work. In most other cases the mage in question thinks something along the lines of \u201cthey can clearly work magick, but they ain't doing it right!\u201c or \u201cof course their way of doing it is viable, but I am more comfortable with my way.\u201c up to \u201cCool! Would you mind to explain the underlying laws of your practice to me? I totally want to learn it/assimilate it into my Sttyle.\u201c<br /> <br /> You can change/broaden your Focus (instrument easy, practice doable, paradigm hard) given time and motivation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T02:22:45-07:00","id":992302,"title":"","content":"Great answers people, I think I have it now. This will hopefully open some really good conversations in our game !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T02:56:21-07:00","id":992306,"title":"","content":"Although, one thing I have to add - all my players at the moment are almost done with the character creation BUT all of them struggle with FOCUS part of the creation - that's literaly the last thing they have to do and none of them understand how to work it out.. :-/ I'm still struggling with explanations for every single paradigmatic choice of theirs. Basically they don't know how to use their paradigm to cast spells. As an example, one person chose Everything is an Illusion, Prison, or Mistake -&gt; The Art of Desire, and asked me - how do I make magic happen with this? From my point every mage desires to hurl magic, so ..'I meditate and want to unlock this door with matter, therefore it's open'?? This thing is really harder for us to overcome than we thought it will!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T03:18:10-07:00","id":992311,"title":"","content":"This is one of the parts of M20's Focus rules that requires a bit of player and storyteller thinking. Because the idea of Everything is an Illusion, Prison, or Mistake can mean different things for different people. As can the Art of Desire.<br /> <br /> The best way to handle this is to ask what that means to the player. If Reality is an illusion/prison/mistake, in what way is it like that? How does their character think the world works? What's their view of cosmology? Granted, this requires one to really think about philosophy, which can be difficult for anyone who has never considered the subject. Really, the various Paradigms, Practices, and Instruments that M20 lists are broad outlines for what should be a more cohesive, more integrated, and more personalized whole.<br /> <br /> To try to brainstorm ideas for this particular example, the Mage character believes that what they see is a lie, or a fabrication, or is simply dictated by arbitrary rules because it was never meant to be. Which of these the Mage believes in is very important, as it informs how they would use their Art of Desire to exploit reality's nature. With the Art of Desire, the character uses their Instruments to either give a person what they desire (even if it's a promise unfulfilled in the end), or to embody qualities people find desirable. It's about knowing people, how they tick, and what influences them. In many ways, using the Art of Desire is like using mundane techniques that affable people use to win friends and influence people, but in such a way that they have a supernatural edge. Wearing all the best clothing, waving sweet-smelling flowers around or putting on scents, speaking in compelling manners, employing body language, maintaining eye contact, establishing ties with people, swearing promises and drafting contracts, etc.<br /> <br /> It would be much easier to know what the character's Tradition is, as this will inform the cultural framework we're working with. A Hermetic approaches the Art of Desire differently than an Ecstasy Cultist, or a Verbana, or a Syndicate rep. Moreover, they all have their own definitions about what it means for Everything to be Illusion, etc.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if I'm not being very helpful. Once you've figured out the wavelength that Mage is running on, it becomes easier to dig into these broad catagories and make a workable Focus from them. But until then, it's a lot of heady business. Abstract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T04:00:50-07:00","id":992321,"title":"","content":"Perhaps it would be better to start with an example Focus. This one is an idea I've been toying with for a while now.<br /> <br /> A member of the Cult of Ecstasy who mixes a vague understanding of Hindu/Buddhist mysticism (namely the idea of Everything is an Illusion, Prison, or Mistake), with the works of Lewis Carroll. From their viewpoint, the world around them is a huge dream that sleeping humanity is having. Going to sleep (or traversing the Umbra) is a matter of traveling into deeper levels of dream, but they are nonetheless still &quot;sleeping&quot; even when awake. There is another level beyond them that is true wakefulness, and that each lifetime a person lives is actually a &quot;night&quot; they spend in slumber and in dream.<br /> <br /> The world is an illusion because it is the fancy of sleeping minds. Mages are simply those that break from the narrative, and become lucid dreamers. As such, all Magick is merely the act of taking control of the dream and bending it to their whim.<br /> <br /> So how does this loony make that happen? Mostly using Crazy Wisdom, but we'll apply a little Art of Desire as well. There is, after all, something alluring about madness. Dressed in Victorian fashion, he swaggers around in a velvet coat, lacy cravat, a poppy blossom in the front pocket, and colorfully painted cane. Hair disheveled but glossy, eyes bobbing from wild to misty. Offering cookies labeled with phrases like &quot;Eat Me&quot;. Speaking softly into someone's ear. Reciting poetry that doesn't make a lick of sense, but a manner that is pleasing to listen to regardless. A simply moving and speaking in an airy, weightless way, as if proclaiming that the forces and laws of the local environment are but suggestions.<br /> <br /> All these things not only get into people's heads when they are around the Cultist, but actually gets into the head of the Dream itself, reshaping it.<br /> <br /> As for Crazy Wisdom, the Cultist knows that it's all a dream, so they work to promote dream logic. Symbols are used heavily. Everyday - and not-so-everyday - objects manipulated in strange ways, as a means of getting across ideas more in line with what the Mage wants. Playing cards and dice and other games of chance or skill. Mirrors and storybook illustrations. Fresh produce and kitchen utensils. Fans and cups and items procured from exotic lands. Magick is driven by metaphor, as are dreams.<br /> <br /> Puns serve much the same purpose, bending wordplay towards unconventional correlations, so that they may be used for Sympathetic Magic. Cracking an egg in order to crack a safe. Running wire for summoning fire. An Ace of Spades, for curing AIDS. Or is that facilitating trades?<br /> <br /> Meditation, for a dreamer, is very like daydreaming. So why can't the Cultist sit and spin images and actions in their head, and have them leak out to infect the outer world? Dreams are dreams, and the divisions between levels of dream can blur together. And there's nothing like having a nap and lucid dreaming to jump off into wanderings through the dreamlands. And, from there, to greater and more wondrous Astral realms.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, simply announcing loudly that the world will change in some way or another can be enough to alter the course of the dream. If you insist, the rocks might decide there's no reason for them not to suddenly be butter. Logic and proportion don't mean anything at all, so butter the rocks shall be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T04:20:29-07:00","id":992323,"title":"","content":"The character in question has chosen and Orphan with several spheres on 2 dots: mind, matter, prime and time. His focus is : Paradigm: Everything is a illusion, Practice: Art of desire, Instruments: Elements ( he chose this one for me to try and come up with a magic effect which is ARGH how do I do it atm ) <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T04:31:33-07:00","id":992325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=992323#post992323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character in question has chosen and Orphan with several spheres on 2 dots: mind, matter, prime and time. His focus is : Paradigm: Everything is a illusion, Practice: Art of desire, Instruments: Elements ( he chose this one for me to try and come up with a magic effect which is ARGH how do I do it atm ) <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's your first problem. They chose an Orphan.<br /> <br /> The reason why other posters advocated starting with a specific Tradition is because it creates an archetype the player can work with as a base. From there, it becomes easier to work the character into their own person. A Hermetic character is a wizard; now the player decides what <i>kind</i> of wizard they want to play. An Akashic character is a mystic martial artist; what kind of kung fu type person does the player want them to be?<br /> <br /> Orphans are difficult for new players because they need to build their concept completely from scratch. And that IS hard.<br /> <br /> If character generation isn't too far gone, you might want to talk to the player about switching to a non-Orphan, and onto a more established Mage archetype. The nine Traditions offer a wealth of potential types to choose from. Witches, shamans, mad scientists, Sudhus and yogis, miracle workers, super hackers, etc. It'll be a lot easier to figure out what Instruments the character would use to perform a particular Effect when popular culture and legend have paved the way so thoroughly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T04:49:34-07:00","id":992331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=992325#post992325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there's your first problem. They chose an Orphan.<br /> <br /> The reason why other posters advocated starting with a specific Tradition is because it creates an archetype the player can work with as a base. From there, it becomes easier to work the character into their own person. A Hermetic character is a wizard; now the player decides what <i>kind</i> of wizard they want to play. An Akashic character is a mystic martial artist; what kind of kung fu type person does the player want them to be?<br /> <br /> Orphans are difficult for new players because they need to build their concept completely from scratch. And that IS hard.<br /> <br /> If character generation isn't too far gone, you might want to talk to the player about switching to a non-Orphan, and onto a more established Mage archetype. The nine Traditions offer a wealth of potential types to choose from. Witches, shamans, mad scientists, Sudhus and yogis, miracle workers, super hackers, etc. It'll be a lot easier to figure out what Instruments the character would use to perform a particular Effect when popular culture and legend have paved the way so thoroughly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You're right - It's not far at all - we're stuck and trying to figure out how to work it out - I will try to nudge him into a tradition character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T05:08:09-07:00","id":992337,"title":"","content":"Elements-as-Instruments (as opposed to Elements-as-Forces-controlled) are employed in ways relevant to the style of the Mage, obviously. But it involves getting a certain amount of the Element together and doing something with it.<br /> <br /> Fire: Candles lit in a circular pattern for spirit summoning. A torch wielded as a weapon (that the magick enhances). A bonfire whipped up until the smoke rises into the air, promoting the formation of storm clouds. A match lit and thrown at a person or object, to set them on fire. Holding a lit candle in one hand, in order to drive away cold. Waving hands in front of a fire in order to manipulate shadows. Enhancing a butane torch so it cuts through steel like butter. Lighting a cigarette to influence minds into thinking you're cool. Staring into a fire and reading the future in the flickering flames. Bearing a lamp to banish the darkness of ignorance. Casting sacrifices into a fire, to propitiate spirits and/or gods of an area relevant to your desires.<br /> <br /> Water: Holy water harming demons and vampires. A vial of water from one's home town, so that the town may protect you from harm. Sprinkling water around an area to purify it. Drinking fresh water to nourish the body and heal wounds. A still pool used for scrying. Diving into a body of water in one location, and surfacing in a different body of water entirely. Draining a bottle into a dry patch of dirt into order to cause a spring to bubble up. Using a spray bottle to create a thick, obscuring mist. Adding thrice distilled water to an alchemical concoction. Raising a glass of water to promote good cheer. Dumping a bucket on a blaze, causing the fire to rapidly die. Drenching oneself with sea water, so as to transform partially into an ocean animal. Promoting a plant's growth along a specific path by watering it in an unusual way.<br /> <br /> Air: Holding a bundle of balloons, in order to float through the air, weightless. Walking with the wind in order to drastically shorten travel time. Predicting the future in the clouds. Piloting a hot air balloon so high, you float into the Umbra. Blowing a handful of sand out in front of you, to summon a gale. Climbing to a high altitude, using the thinner air to promote an altered mental state. Performing a rite in a large, open area.<br /> <br /> Earth: Surrounding oneself with a circle of stones, to ward against spirits. Keeping a rock in one's pocket, to channel its strength and endurance. Bearing a pebble of turquois, to manipulate the sea and sky. Erecting stone columns, Stonehenge style, in order to establish a Node. Chucking a rock at a set of scaffolding, so that it breaks just the way you want it to. Surrounding your bed with dirt from your birthplace, to promote sound sleep. Looking through a hunk of crystal, to see into the world of spirits. Rubbing sand into a sturdy surface, until it begins to crumble. Covering yourself with mud, so as to cancel your heat signature from thermal detection devices. Breaking a building's cornerstone, that it will eventually collapse into ruin. Meditating on a pebble, to achieve insight.<br /> <br /> <br /> I can keep going with more unconventional elements, like Electricity, Glass, Plastic, Metal, Wood, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T05:36:40-07:00","id":992339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=992306#post992306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, one thing I have to add - all my players at the moment are almost done with the character creation BUT all of them struggle with FOCUS part of the creation - that's literaly the last thing they have to do and none of them understand how to work it out.. :-/ I'm still struggling with explanations for every single paradigmatic choice of theirs. Basically they don't know how to use their paradigm to cast spells. As an example, one person chose Everything is an Illusion, Prison, or Mistake -&gt; The Art of Desire, and asked me - how do I make magic happen with this? From my point every mage desires to hurl magic, so ..'I meditate and want to unlock this door with matter, therefore it's open'?? This thing is really harder for us to overcome than we thought it will!</div> </div> </div> </div>The first thing I've noticed is that the player in question only has 2 of the 3 pieces of their focus Paradigm (Everything is an Illusion, Prison, or Mistake) and Art of Desire (Practice) but Im not seeing any Instruments and that last part is the closest to the actual <i>how </i>in terms of what the Mages does to cast their spells. However lets look at the first two and see if we can't piece it together.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradigm (Everything is an Illusion, Prison or Mistake) </b>- The question your player has to answer here is how they view the world through the lens of this paradigm. Some possible interpretations below (note this doesnt have to be <i>true </i>your Mage just has to believe it).<ul><li>The world is a mistake, the rounding error of an immensely powerful being and it there was no significance in its creation (a very Lovecraftian perspective)</li> <li>The world is a creation of a (or many) evil entities (malfeans, the devil, etc) to act as an experiment on lesser beings</li> <li>The world is a prison either for humanity or for something else and humanity is just caught in the crossfire</li> <li>The world is a test, an exam from a powerful entity (god, angels, incarnae, etc) that humanity must 'pass' before they can ascend beyond the mortal state</li> </ul><br /> No matter which of these (or some other permutation I didn't come up with, that list is no mean exhaustive) there is some deeper truth which the Mage is trying to see to and use to make their will manifest. Depending on which of these they choose will add flavor to their casting and magic. The Mage that thinks the world is a prison for humanity has a much darker and depressing view of the truth than someone who thinks the world being an illusion is a test for humanity.<br /> <br /> <b>Practice (Art of Desire) and Instruments (None chosen)- </b>These two are closely related. The Practice is the overall binding element for the Mages instruments it also gives practical form and methodology to the Mage's Paradigm. The Art of Desire is all about finding out other peoples desires and using that to enact your own desires. Its a very 'big business' view of doing magick, as the believer of <i>Ars Cupidae </i>is coming up with a grand plan than looks at those who would buy into that plan and how to sell it to them to reach their goals. The Instruments are the bits and pieces which make the Mages Practice function and the actual 'stuff' they do to make the magick happen. Remember that until a Mage becomes very powerful these are things they must do to cast their spells or they take penalties for fast casting or working without instruments. The problem is I don't know whether your mage views the reality behind the illusion as benevolent or not so it makes it harder to flavor the Practice and Instruments, but Ill try to provide thoughts on both.<br /> <br /> <b>Art of Desire (The truth about reality is benevolent or neutral)</b><br /> People want things because deep down they know that this isn't all there is, there is something more. Your Mage has started to see what lies beyond the material world we live in and has started to manipulate theirs and others desires to pierce the illusion and make their will manifest. Looking at some of the common instruments, note that the Sphere(s) you use may change how you use the instruments to cast the spell. When casting a spell your Mage will often use multiple Instruments to make it happen, combining them to get the effect they want. I also put the Sphere(s) I think work best with a particular instrument at the end of my description.<ul><li>Cards and dice - Fate and probability manipulators, your Mage has a goal and you want to push the outcomes to what you expect versus what may be likely to occur. As you are casting the spell you might have to roll the dice (maybe multiple times) or play a game of solitaire as you try to push the outcome of the rolls/game to match what you want to happen. They might also function as a representation of resources (the cards remaining unused in Solitaire or the deck in a game of poker for example). Sphere(s): Entropy, Prime.</li> <li>Cosmetics - Its about using makeup and prostheses to make yourself or others look the way you want them to change to be or trying to draw a particular reaction from a target. The casting of the spell involves applying the makeup and prostheses until the look matches what you want. Sphere(s): Life, Mind</li> <li>(Very refined) Dance and Gestures - Dancing may be about drawing a particular person a certain way or getting them into a certain move. Gestures can be anything from kissing a ladies hand to slapping someone in the face with a glove. Its about provoking reactions leading to your goal or watching and manipulating the flow of a dance to get what you want. When casting you dance or perform the appropriate gestures necessary for what you want. Sphere(s) Correspondence, Mind</li> <li>Eye contact - To try to figure out what someone wants you have to look at them. Additionally there is the adage about the eyes being the windows to the soul and by looking someone directly in the eyes you are forging a connection with them. How you make eye contact can also alter the vibe of the contact as making bedroom eyes at someone is a different feel than looking at someone with an angry deathglare. Eye contact will almost always be part of casting a spell involving a particular person. Sphere(s): Mind</li> <li>Fashion - The 'power' suit, the little black dress, the white tie tuxedo, the face hiding hoodie, military uniforms all these are particular looks which inspire an image and idea about the person wearing them. There is the adage 'dress for the job you want not the job you have' the masters of the Art of Desire have taken this to heart in regards to casting spells. If your character wants to cast a spell to wow someone to get them to do what they want they might dress to impress; where as if they wanted to cast a spell to protect themselves in combat they will wear body armor to inspire fear and respect. Casting the spell will involve choosing and putting on the outfit or showing it off in the way to produce the desired effect. Sphere(s) Life, Matter (altering the materials for protection)</li> <li>Gadgets - The catch all for the various items the Mage uses to represent the effects and devices needed for their spells. Its broad to cover the areas the other instruments might not, and are especially important to Technocracy and technology based Mages. Specifically to the Art of Desire a couple that come to mind - the cellphone/little black book with all the contacts the Mage might need to call, online appraisal/ebay lookup to determine the value (or value the mage sets) on an item or location. Sphere(s) All</li> <li>Mass media - Using the power of TV, Radio, Print, Online media to gauge what people want or make them want or not want something. The product jingle comes to mind, the little song that sticks in your head and makes sure you remember the product when you go to the store. Another example is the fear mongering attack ad, if you vote for them the terrorists win. Useful when used in conjunction with larger effects that affect multiple people. Sphere(s): Correspondence, Mind</li> <li>Money and wealth - Money is power and buying happiness and what you want, paying people to do what you want, a physical representation of value. Money can be used when casting a spell to affect a particular person. It can also be useful for applying value to a certain object or thing. Practitioners of the Art of Desire are likely to view quintessence and tass in terms of wealth, a weak node might be called a fixer-upper where a powerful one might be called a lucrative investment. When casting the spell you might be paying the person or transferring the funds, even something as simple as looking up values or counting money can work too. Sphere(s) Mind, Prime</li> <li>Sex - Without getting into the racy details, sex is about manipulating or providing someone one of the base desires of a majority of people. Tantric sex or the quickie could also fall under the purview of an Art of Desire Mage. Sphere(s) Life, Mind</li> <li>Social domination - Celebrities, the Diss/Insult, the secret tape, the dirty secret. Using a greater social standing to get people to do what you want or making sure people help or hinder a particular target or goal. Casting the spell will involve crafting the tweet, mass mail, or insult/praise to get the desired reaction. Sphere(s): Mind</li> <li>Vehicles - What you drive can be as important as how you drive it. A limo or high end luxury car is going to send a much different message than a black SUV or a beat up station wagon and a wise user of the Art of Desire can make great use of this advantage. Vehicles are also symbolic of travel and distances and can be used to manipulate such (your flight just happens to be early or your rivals flight gets delayed. Casting may involve driving to a location and getting out or booking the flight or looking up a person's flight plans. Sphere(s): Correspondence, Mind</li> <li>Voice - Its how you articulate what you want; whether its a question, statement, or threat. The right words in the right place or ear can make all the difference between going forward with an idea or one being left on the cutting room floor. Casting the spell might be asking someone what they want, shouting and insulting an opponent, or just making a statement regarding something (I'm reminded of the Doctor Who moment where the Doctor says &quot;Doesn't she look tired&quot; which ends up leading to her defeat from politics). Sphere(s): All</li> <li>Weapons - The various tools of war which the Mage will likely use when casting combat effects or intimidate or reassure. Sphere(s): Forces, Mind</li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:51:41-07:00","id":992383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=992323#post992323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character in question has chosen and Orphan with several spheres on 2 dots: mind, matter, prime and time. His focus is : Paradigm: Everything is a illusion, Practice: Art of desire, Instruments: Elements ( he chose this one for me to try and come up with a magic effect which is ARGH how do I do it atm ) <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Everything above is perfectly applicable and certainly worth consideration. But just as a counterpoint (as well as a small challenge for myself) I'm going to try and think up a Focus with the criteria provided.<br /> <br /> They are an Orphan<br /> They have two dots in Mind, Matter, Prime, and Time (wow that's a lot for a starting mage!)<br /> Paradigm is Everything is an Illusion<br /> Practice is Art of Desire<br /> Instruments are the Elements<br /> <br /> Step one, the Paradigm: As Cynic01 correctly states, you need to understand from your player what they actually consider the world to be in terms of illusion. But as long as it's established that the world we see is not the world that is, then we're good to go.<br /> <br /> Step two, the Practice: Art of Desire. This actually fits in to the above Paradigm pretty well. Perhaps the Orphan mage thinks that the world is only what people want to see in it. So if they're negative and enjoy bashing how nothing works, then their desire for pulling things apart literally manifests in systems falling apart all around them, the bus is always late, the printer always jams, nepotism will always keep you away from your promotion, and going to the doctor will always cause bad news and terrible ailments to manifest.<br /> Conversely, perhaps they think a positive outlook and a desire to see the good in the world will cause positive things to manifest around them. A kind man helps a lost child reunite with their searching mother, the sun comes out just before a party in the park, you meet someone at a bus stop and you just seem to click.<br /> This viewpoint is somewhat a combination of the &quot;rule of 3&quot; from Wicca, and the Karmic cycle, where what you expect colours what you desire to see, and what you desire shapes what the world provides for you. When you're a sleeper, you let what the world provides for you colour your expectations, creating a closed loop of self perpetuation. But when you're awakened, you're able to break out of this loop, and focus your desires properly to create the outcome of events you actually want.<br /> <br /> So most people expect matter to be solid, and so subconsciously desire it to be solid, therefor matter is solid. Your mage, however, knows that if they can truly focus their desire for the matter to be less solid, reality will abide and change.<br /> <br /> Step three: the Focus: Here's how we can get the elements to fit into all of this: Think about the minor arcana of the Tarot. There are four suits each corresponding to one of the four elements.<br /> <br /> Wands: Fire<br /> Cups: Water<br /> Swords: Air<br /> Coins: Earth<br /> <br /> However, they also correspond to different ways of being.<br /> <br /> Wands/Fire: Action &amp; Creation<br /> Cups/Water: Emotion &amp; Passion<br /> Swords/Air: Intellect &amp; Reasoning<br /> Coins/Earth: Instinct &amp; Intuition<br /> <br /> These different modes of thought can be used to shape the way one enacts their desire on the world, and thus creates the effect they wish to see. The focus itself can be a symbol for them to focus that area of their desire into being.<br /> <br /> So if they need to create something, perhaps it comes out of the burning embers of something else. Burning a log in order to find a number of coins within it (Matter 2), or using the flickering light of a flame and its constant dance to focus their desire upon another's mind, creating an impulse within them (Mind 2).<br /> The cold feeling of water on their skin may allow them to tap into the emotional side of their desire, and create a connection so powerful with whatever they are looking at that they can look into their future (Time 2).<br /> Maybe they need to go outside into an evening breeze to clear their head enough to think rationally, allowing them to properly move Quintessential energy into their own body (Prime 2) or provide greater strength to their weapons (also Prime 2).<br /> Maybe they feel the need to ground themselves, literally, burying their feat in the earth so they can tap into that instinctual side of themselves, allowing them to intuitively feel out time (Time 1) or simply know what something is made of (Matter 1).<br /> <br /> These are just some examples, if your player likes them, then they are free to think any others that would fit in this system.<br /> <br /> Additionally, they aren't limited to the elements in their &quot;raw&quot; form, but could use icons as representations of them. This could be as simple as using the tarot symbols themselves (wands, cups, swords, and coins) or objects that are associated with these elements (Candle, Bottle, Balloon, Plant pot), or even objects that resemble these elements, such as gems (Jasper, Sodalite, Opal, Jet) or Nature (Fang, Shell, Feather, Claw). As long as it makes sense to the orphan why these particular objects can be used, and how they can help in focusing their desire in specific ways. It can't be arbitrary.<br /> <br /> The key here is that the element used puts them in the correct frame of mind to amplify their desire on to reality, breaking the illusion and resulting in real physical change.7<br /> <br /> How's that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 10-24-2016, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:20:27-07:00","id":992908,"title":"","content":"That's more than enough haha, cheers mate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T03:45:20-07:00","id":994484,"title":"","content":"Eh, well - my players still really struggle with paradigm. At this stage we had 3 meetings where I tried my best to explain this, all of them read the chapters in m20 about this but still can't finish their characters and I'm unable to reach a point where we even can begin a game. So this begs for a question - is it possible to play this game without the paradigm/focus part? And if so, what steps are necessary to make it playable?<br /> <br /> I must admit it has put a dent in my optimism towards my gm skills and this game but there is still hoping","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T03:56:30-07:00","id":994486,"title":"","content":"Don't loose Hope.<br /> Of course you can begin play without Focus.<br /> This is a game after all. <br /> There isn't a team of OnyxPath orthodoxy enforcers coming for you if you deviate from the standard.<br /> <br /> In this case it would be helpful to pick a few signature effects for each PC and flesh them out.<br /> Begin play and wait how it goes.<br /> Learning by doing is very magey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T05:41:56-07:00","id":994511,"title":"","content":"You could always write up characters yourself, and have them play those. Characters who hedge closely to a Mage archetype. While this does mean your players have to play pre-generated characters, it also means they have a role they can begin play as. Maybe with a list of rotes they prefer, with descriptions of how they perform them and the rationale behind it.<br /> <br /> It doesn't need to be an extended chronicle. A short game that lasts a couple sessions at best is just fine. And it gives the players a way to work through the game. If having too much freedom in a system that is so open-ended is the problem, maybe it would help to start in a more limited environment. Moreover, if you make the pre-gens simple enough, the players can begin fleshing them out, and expanding beyond the rotes they have. They can experiment. In that case, the limits work to your advantage, as it can foster creativity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T05:54:41-07:00","id":994516,"title":"","content":"Creating characters or casting magic is not an issue - the only problem is that they all created mages but can't cope with the paradigm - at this stage I don't know if they don't like and act ignorance or really can't finish their toons with focus. We did 2 hrs of casting magic - where they could explain creative spells without focus but struggle when it comes to link those two. Even with fantastic examples in this threads - they seem unconvinced and asked me if we could play mage without that part of the book. One guy actually left the group because of this discussions *sigh*. Even If I create 4 different paradigms for them - they will struggle to play it out in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T05:58:03-07:00","id":994521,"title":"","content":"In a way that's probably my fault as I've oversold the system to them claiming you can do everything - wheras now it seems that they need to dance, have sex and wave wands and what not and they're not happy with that :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T07:06:26-07:00","id":994548,"title":"","content":"If a rule is getting in the way of having fun, then the rule isn't worth the hassle. At the end of the day, it's about doing what's best for the group.<br /> That being said, I would agree that to ignore the paradigm aspect of mage is a real shame as it's one of the most interesting sources of conflict there is.<br /> <br /> My current crop of players were completely new to Mage as well. I'm not sure if this will be of any use to you at this stage, but here's what I did for them.<br /> <br /> At Character Creation, I worked on them with their character individually. As in, I invited one of the players over and the day was dedicated to only that person's Character.<br /> I asked them if they had an idea for a character in mind, and listened to what they said.<br /> If they didn't, we'd start from scratch, and either begin with Roleplay or Stats depending on what they felt more comfortable with.<br /> <br /> Stats is pretty self explanatory, we chose the Concept, Nature, Demeanour and Essence, shown them the list of Traditions, I give the numbers and ran through what each stat actually did. Everything right up until the Advantages and Spheres section.<br /> <br /> Roleplay first means I ask them a bunch of questions to try and figure out what we know about this guy. How old are they? What's their dayjob? Do they have any family... That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Either the stats help inform these answers, or these answers help inform the stats, either way works.<br /> <br /> There are, however, three questions I always ask my players, and I do not accept anything less than a well thought out answer.<br /> <br /> How did your mage Awaken?<br /> How does your mage think the universe works?<br /> When your mage does magic, what do they think they are doing?<br /> <br /> These three questions are key to how I got my Players to work out their paradigm.<br /> The first allows them to put their character in the context of the setting. it forces the player to consider the difference between their Sleeper player and what changed. This change is how they became aware of Magic, but not only that, but on how they realised that reality wasn't as static as they had once thought before. It also forces the player to contextualise the tradition they associated with, and may even give allegiances towards a particular faction within the tradition.<br /> <br /> The second is the key point of paradigm. I never showed my players the M20 book on Focus. Sure it's a nice source which lays things out pretty nicely, but it made the whole thing feel more like a flowchart than a personal field of view. If they were going to understand their paradigm properly, it would have to come from them.<br /> I do not give too much guidance on this, I let them look through the tradition's various beliefs and encourage them to ask me questions on how to go about this, but at the end of the day, this answer has to come from them.<br /> <br /> The third question is how to get their Practice sorted out. Now that the player has a concrete idea of how they think reality works, they can consider what the mage is able to do to alter it.<br /> Here are my players as examples.<br /> <br /> - One thinks the universe is basically all constructed out of data and code, so if they can hack into the values that structure reality, they can change said reality, much like one would mod a videogame.<br /> - One believes that the universe is nothing but a swirling maelstrom of chaos, and any semblance of consistency is just an illusion created by the observer to make themselves feel better. Because they are aware of this, they are able dispel this illusion and return the natural chaos to them, or even take control of this chaos and force a specific kind of order into it, In this way they can make changes in the way reality appears to work, and in a reality that is nothing but illusions anyway, that's exactly the same thing as makings things change.<br /> - One thinks that the rhythm of life is made on the backbone of language, and that all things are part of an ongoing narrative. If then, they can place specific portions of narrative, words, or rhythms into the right place at the right time, they can force a level of change to take place in the story that plays out before them.<br /> - One does not believe that magic is inherent to humans, but is actually a form of divine intervention. When he does magic, he is actually acting as a conduit for the Will of the Divine.<br /> <br /> They all came up with those themselves, no guide necessary.<br /> <br /> Anyway, once this is all thought up, it is then and only then that we go through things like the Spheres. We finish up their character sheets, and before going on to Merits and Flaws, we look at &quot;Tools&quot;. Now each player knows exactly what they are doing with magic, and which spheres are under their influence.<br /> The next question is &quot;How dose you character actually do magic then?&quot;<br /> <br /> This is the only time I let them look at the list of tool's to give them idea of what is available, and remind them that this list is not exclusive. They are allowed to use any tool they like so long as they are able to explain to me how it fits in with the paradigm and practice they though about earlier.<br /> <br /> For the Computer guy, it only makes sense that his tools be various pieces of software for his computer, smart phone, or tablet.<br /> For Maelstrom guy, he needs to get his mind into focus to deal with the chaos, so he turns to alcohol. If he can loosen himself up a bit, getting his head on the same track as the chaos around him, then things get a lot easier.<br /> For Language guy, it's all about the words, poetry, and language. He has a number of wooden Runes which he uses to spell ancient words of forgotten lore, he can also recite poems in a rhythmic process to impose specific kinds of narratives to take place around him.<br /> For Religious guy, he is simply paying tribute to his Deity, and in so doing is able to garner their favour. A Prayer for help gives help. A request for the tools needed to vanquish foes is provided. Holding his cross in hand allows him to commune with a divine sense allowing him to feel out what he is searching for.<br /> <br /> Then we cover everything else, go through Merits and Flaws, and that's it, all done.<br /> <br /> Another question I might ask them is &quot;How aware if your mage of his Avatar?&quot; and then try to figure out what that relationship is like. This can be done as early as talking about Essence, or as late as the last thing you do. But it's an important part of Mage. How aware they are, as well as how their avatar interacts with them shouldn't be glossed over.<br /> <br /> <br /> The important things are as follows:<br /> 1. It's a one-on-one meeting with the ST and the player. This allows them to create a very individualised idea of how magic functions. If they are all in the same room, then it becomes all too easy to laps into a shared belief system, and the ever present Purple Paradigm.<br /> 2. You can't look at tools without knowing how they affect reality, and you can't know how to affect reality unless you know what reality is and how it functions. This must be done in this order, and they have an internal logic to them. If they don't, then the paradigm doesn't work. Be strict about this, if something doesn't make sense to the player, then it can't possibly function for the character.<br /> 3. Do your utmost best not to lead the player to a paradigm. The more it comes from them, the more willing they will be to defend it like their Mage character would do.<br /> 4. Think about their avatar. It is the best ST tool in the whole game.<br /> <br /> One thing I might suggest is, if your Players are really having a hard time getting their head around Paradigm, and it's gone to the point that you can't do a thing about it. But they are still interesting in playing a free-form magic game. Why not try out Mage: The Awakening?<br /> <br /> That system has every mage have more or less the same paradigm, they just bicker about the &quot;best&quot; or most &quot;efficient&quot; means of producing magic.<br /> Sure, there's no technocracy, and very little lore by comparison, but it might work as an alternative route into the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 10-29-2016, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T07:20:57-07:00","id":994558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=994516#post994516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating characters or casting magic is not an issue - the only problem is that they all created mages but can't cope with the paradigm - at this stage I don't know if they don't like and act ignorance or really can't finish their toons with focus. We did 2 hrs of casting magic - where they could explain creative spells without focus but struggle when it comes to link those two. Even with fantastic examples in this threads - they seem unconvinced and asked me if we could play mage without that part of the book. One guy actually left the group because of this discussions *sigh*. Even If I create 4 different paradigms for them - they will struggle to play it out in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems you have to try to determine something important here - Are they being purposefully ignorant of Focus or do they really not 'get' it? <br /> <br /> If its purposefully ignoring it that feels disrespectful to the work you've put into the game as the ST. The ST is the one who has the hard job of creating the world, populating it with NPCs, and setting up plotlines, generally that means the players should try to work with them in regards to rules and structure of the game. If you think that; you should talk to your players on that issue because its likely to become a problem again when they run into something they dont like.<br /> <br /> If its 'not getting it' then there are some ways around that.<br /> <br /> Its hard to just remove instruments because they have an intrinsic mechanical effect (a penalty when not used).<br /> <br /> The solution that comes to my mind is you work with the player to select 7 Instruments (as per the rules) that fit what they have chosen for Practice and then tie them to a specific Sphere (this means 2 of the instruments get to be used for an additional Sphere). Then the Mage either has to have the object in question on their person or be able to physically do the action when casting a spell using the Sphere(s) in question or they take the penalty for working without or with unfamiliar instrument, but dont have to describe how they use it. Also the rules say a Mage can discard 1 instrument when reaching Arete 4 and each dot thereafter.<br /> <br /> However it seems a shame and disservice to the game to remove the Focus. The Ascension War between Traditions and Technocrats is being fought over Focus. As stated no roleplaying police are going to break through your wall and tell you that you are doing it wrong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T07:02:08-07:00","id":995178,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2008\" data-vbnamecard=\"2008\">Cynic01</a> I never stated that no roleplaying police breaks through...<br /> I just said that no OnyxPath orthodoxy enforcers are coming.<br /> The devil is in the details...<br /> <br /> Ok back to seriousness again, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> worded it very good. <br /> Another thing that comes to mind is giving all the players the merit from Initiates of the art (forgot the name 7 points, use any practice and instrument that got explained to you) for free. Also give anyone one dot in Mentor.<br /> Now give everyone a Focus(the one imparted by their mentor) if later in play a player whishes to change his Focus or parts of it it is no problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T09:20:46-07:00","id":995235,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, good news! <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> advice of the 3 questions pushed things forward - we did a individual q&amp;a session and managed to get 2 characters sorted with individual focus! Two remain. Will keep you posted :-) Much obliged for all your responses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T09:32:03-07:00","id":995239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=995178#post995178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2008\" data-vbnamecard=\"2008\">Cynic01</a> I never stated that no roleplaying police breaks through...<br /> I just said that no OnyxPath orthodoxy enforcers are coming.<br /> The devil is in the details...<br /> <br /> Ok back to seriousness again, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> worded it very good.<br /> Another thing that comes to mind is giving all the players the merit from Initiates of the art (forgot the name 7 points, use any practice and instrument that got explained to you) for free. Also give anyone one dot in Mentor.<br /> Now give everyone a Focus(the one imparted by their mentor) if later in play a player whishes to change his Focus or parts of it it is no problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd bootstrap off this. If they aren't be deliberately obtuse and not getting it because they don't want to because they don't want any limitations on what they can do (and this can definitely be an issue when players are used to games where maximizing potential is part of the objective) or you oversold that aspect of Mage and that's their (reasonable?) expectation, then setting things up so they all have a role model (aka Mentor) who can demonstrate Practice and Instruments might work pretty well. Then you can start with some Instruments that the teacher and student can share and the Mentor can coach them in a few that are specific to the character. It might work even better if the characters can share Mentors, up to the point of having just one for the entire group. Single Tradition games can be loads of fun. (We did a space-faring SoE game that still stands head and shoulders above many many other Mage games across a couple of decades.)<br /> <br /> Honestly, the worst players in the worst Mage games I've experienced, even back to the days of 1st Ed weirdness have been the number-crunching wish-crafters who say, &quot;I use Forces 3 and Prime 2 and create a fireball. What's my Diff?&quot; Particularly when the other players are trying hard to get more into the spirit of the game, it can really bring the whole thing to a crashing halt. If the character is deliberately doing this, it will usually get something along the line of, &quot;Well, that's Vulgar with Witnesses. You are fast-casting and surpassing your focus/using an unfamiliar instrument. So, that's... Difficulty 12.... So, Difficulty 9 with a 3 success Threshold.&quot; Note, however, such players have been those who seem to have the most fun when they are making the game less fun for everyone else.<br /> <br /> If you want a game of reality-ripping wish-crafters who border on Marauder-dom or who exist in world where that's what Mages ARE, you can toss Focus completely. It's a different sort of game. It would probably work best with mages being about as rare as hen's teeth and no need for such things as Affiliations beyond the very very broad. (Nephandi vs. Marauders vs. Mages). Then let the players just go around and rip holes in causality with impunity, limited only by the occasional Paradox backlash. Or even have the Focus/Instruments be really really easy without much need to overt explication (like, say, &quot;magic takes odd hand gestures a la the Magicians TV show). Then you don't have to stress about Focus very much, but it can come up from time to time. (Chopping off fingers becomes a REAL threat...)<br /> <br /> That might be fun as Hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T10:15:01-07:00","id":995247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=995239#post995239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd bootstrap off this. If they aren't be deliberately obtuse and not getting it because they don't want to because they don't want any limitations on what they can do (and this can definitely be an issue when players are used to games where maximizing potential is part of the objective) or you oversold that aspect of Mage and that's their (reasonable?) expectation, then setting things up so they all have a role model (aka Mentor) who can demonstrate Practice and Instruments might work pretty well. Then you can start with some Instruments that the teacher and student can share and the Mentor can coach them in a few that are specific to the character. It might work even better if the characters can share Mentors, up to the point of having just one for the entire group. Single Tradition games can be loads of fun. (We did a space-faring SoE game that still stands head and shoulders above many many other Mage games across a couple of decades.)<br /> <br /> Honestly, the worst players in the worst Mage games I've experienced, even back to the days of 1st Ed weirdness have been the number-crunching wish-crafters who say, &quot;I use Forces 3 and Prime 2 and create a fireball. What's my Diff?&quot; Particularly when the other players are trying hard to get more into the spirit of the game, it can really bring the whole thing to a crashing halt. If the character is deliberately doing this, it will usually get something along the line of, &quot;Well, that's Vulgar with Witnesses. You are fast-casting and surpassing your focus/using an unfamiliar instrument. So, that's... Difficulty 12.... So, Difficulty 9 with a 3 success Threshold.&quot; Note, however, such players have been those who seem to have the most fun when they are making the game less fun for everyone else.<br /> <br /> If you want a game of reality-ripping wish-crafters who border on Marauder-dom or who exist in world where that's what Mages ARE, you can toss Focus completely. It's a different sort of game. It would probably work best with mages being about as rare as hen's teeth and no need for such things as Affiliations beyond the very very broad. (Nephandi vs. Marauders vs. Mages). Then let the players just go around and rip holes in causality with impunity, limited only by the occasional Paradox backlash. Or even have the Focus/Instruments be really really easy without much need to overt explication (like, say, &quot;magic takes odd hand gestures a la the Magicians TV show). Then you don't have to stress about Focus very much, but it can come up from time to time. (Chopping off fingers becomes a REAL threat...)<br /> <br /> That might be fun as Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, two of my players are showing incredible enthusiasm about this game - up to the point where Barbara ( only girl in our group ) has finished reading her tradition book, has read the paradigm sections several times, wrote a backstory of her character ( euthanatos ) and is challenging me in creative ways ( I actually want to prepare a whole Diksha event for her now). One guy who is indeed a number crunching gamer has described the paradigm aspect of this game as stupid ( that's after the second discussion about it, he didn't read about it ), so we all have decided it's best if he didn't play - he's gone. There will be two more players, who are not so invested but I know they will make effort once the game begins. We toyed with the idea of one tradition but they decided they liked different things and I'm ok with that. There will be an Euthanatos ( with powerful plot hooks that I can mix in the chronicle - PTSD flaw, amnesia, enemy and more ), a Hermes guy ala young Elon Musk, Verbena doctor that has lost his license ( yet to be established why ), and VA played by a really experienced WOD player ( not really a power gamer but he knows the ins and outs of this systems ). First two got their paradigms finished today and I'm really happy with the results as I can now slowly flesh out some main NPCs and finally focus on everything else before we kick off. We decided to play as per RAW when it comes to character creation : arete 3, skills 3, spheres 3 - they had a lot of fun with backgrounds/merits and flaws ( lots of complaints how many awesome options are at hand, yet so few points available <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) - reason being that I want them to play around with magic and so that they can have a bit more options at the beginning. I will try to be a bit conservative with XP to balance this out. This is where I am now. <br /> <br /> What I have to do now is reread how they should describe using magic, do some reading on rules to make sure I don't make that many mistakes ( I will keep in heart your advice about winging it but keeping the right to correct that decision later if rules were exploited or broken ). I will also use the 'are you sure' advice as this could be handy at the start of our chronicle. I'm still open to any suggestions for a beginner chronicle or session - honestly I can't say how helpful you guys are and how much the last posts helped me out!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T11:59:01-07:00","id":995286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=995247#post995247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, two of my players are showing incredible enthusiasm about this game - up to the point where Barbara ( only girl in our group ) has finished reading her tradition book, has read the paradigm sections several times, wrote a backstory of her character ( euthanatos ) and is challenging me in creative ways ( I actually want to prepare a whole Diksha event for her now). One guy who is indeed a number crunching gamer has described the paradigm aspect of this game as stupid ( that's after the second discussion about it, he didn't read about it ), so we all have decided it's best if he didn't play - he's gone. There will be two more players, who are not so invested but I know they will make effort once the game begins. We toyed with the idea of one tradition but they decided they liked different things and I'm ok with that. There will be an Euthanatos ( with powerful plot hooks that I can mix in the chronicle - PTSD flaw, amnesia, enemy and more ), a Hermes guy ala young Elon Musk, Verbena doctor that has lost his license ( yet to be established why ), and VA played by a really experienced WOD player ( not really a power gamer but he knows the ins and outs of this systems ). First two got their paradigms finished today and I'm really happy with the results as I can now slowly flesh out some main NPCs and finally focus on everything else before we kick off. We decided to play as per RAW when it comes to character creation : arete 3, skills 3, spheres 3 - they had a lot of fun with backgrounds/merits and flaws ( lots of complaints how many awesome options are at hand, yet so few points available <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) - reason being that I want them to play around with magic and so that they can have a bit more options at the beginning. I will try to be a bit conservative with XP to balance this out. This is where I am now.<br /> <br /> What I have to do now is reread how they should describe using magic, do some reading on rules to make sure I don't make that many mistakes ( I will keep in heart your advice about winging it but keeping the right to correct that decision later if rules were exploited or broken ). I will also use the 'are you sure' advice as this could be handy at the start of our chronicle. I'm still open to any suggestions for a beginner chronicle or session - honestly I can't say how helpful you guys are and how much the last posts helped me out!</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be afraid to teach via demonstration:<ul><li>Ask them what the character wants to accomplish.</li> <li>Then give them suggestions about which of their Spheres they could use to do so, with some ways that using different Spheres might accomplish the objective in different ways. (Also some info about whether it's vulgar, whether there a witnesses and, if it's vulgar, an idea about how it might be coincidental if done <i>thusly</i>)</li> <li>Followed by a description of the way that a few of their Instruments would allow them to meet their goals. Including whether this is a flat out role or something of a ritual where success are built up over several rolls. Whether they can build the effect (adding successes by subsequent casting rolls) or they are effectively &quot;holding&quot; the effects until they are done with the casting. .</li> <li>THEN start with calculation of Difficulties, deciding what each success is going to mean, etc.</li> </ul><br /> If you make them a part of the discussion, they are likely to start picking up their part of it and letting you, as ST, know what Spheres they want to use to do X and how it's going to look in game when the character is trying to accomplish that. In many (most) cases, there will always be a give and take between you and the player on setting this up (though it can get pretty fast). That's a part of Mage.<br /> <br /> This isn't just a new player/new ST thing either. Players who have been with my group since the turn of the century will tackle a character with a completely different set-up than anything they have played to date and we work through this. In the current game, one player is a NWO agent (from the early 1960's, so there's another whole set of issues in play as well). He never played a Technocrat. The rest of the group is Tradition mages (well, the VA is actually from when the VAs were part of the Union, but he was something of a iconoclast from back in the day). The character is sort of a MiB CSI, so he has lots of Spheres at 1 dot for detection purposes and specializes in Entropy with some Time. We were at loose ends about what he could do and how it would look for some time. The player was struggling with the character. It didn't seem to be as much fun as the Tradition characters, as he couldn't figure out how to do very much. But we worked through it. It took a few epiphanies for both of us. Now he's the master-planner of the group. He essentially sets up the goal state the group is trying to achieve and thinks of it like a crime scene (e.g. what the situation would look like after they had succeeded) and then works backward to figure out exactly what needs to be done and in what order to achieve that objective. The situation has flipped and now he loves the character. He uses his MiB Crime Scene Kit (i.e. his set of Instruments) and his Sherlock Holmes deductive/inductive theorizing (another Instrument), pops a few &quot;Cognitive Aids&quot; (a.k.a. mind enhancing drugs, another Instrument) and FIGURES IT OUT. (Oh, and it's virtually always coincidental as well....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T12:26:47-07:00","id":995299,"title":"","content":"The stuff about your Euthanatos player, that's awesome! This is the kind of attitude which makes for a very good game.<br /> It's probably a blessing in disguise that your number cruncher left the group, partially because if they're having this much of a hard time with Paradigm, then things are not going to get any easier later on. But also because 4 players is a much more sensible number to deal with. 5 can be a handful, while 6 can become just plain difficult.<br /> <br /> Regarding preset stories, I'm not sure I can help you. I tend to make up all the plots I use. I will however say that it should be in some way linked to the characters made by your players.<br /> <br /> The first thing to do is to think up why all these characters are working together or in the same group. You can do this with your players if you like, perhaps they characters already know each other. Alternatively you could do a prelude session where we learn how they came to meet each other, and thus set up all kinds of plothooks.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Verbena Doctor lost his license because the Euthanatos killed someone under his care and got sued for malpractice, perhaps this patient was a respected Hermetic who was known by the OoH guy, and maybe had a day job working with the VA.<br /> <br /> Maybe the reason this guy had to die is because they were a closet infernalist who was trying to summon demons to do stuff.<br /> <br /> This is just an example of how you could tie these players together and give them a few interesting things discuss. Perhaps each one know a small piece about this one person and they all need to rely on one another's knowledge to find out what's really going on.<br /> <br /> Again, just an example. If you've got a better, or you're not a fan of demon stories, then by all means go with something else.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T18:53:03-07:00","id":995469,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you handled the problem player of your group. Really, if the player had such a problem with the whole Focus aspect of the game, they weren't going to have fun playing Mage. I find that, with Mage: The Ascension, <i>how you do magick</i> is as important, if not more important, than what you do. It's part of the fun, and makes the players more invested in their characters (as opposed to just seeing them as tools for doing neat magic things unto themselves). And if that player was being so much of a pill, it would only detract from everyone's fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for what to do plotwise, ask your players what their characters' long term goals are. These goals should be personal to the character, and create fertile ground for stories. As such, just saying they want to increase their Traits is probably not enough; they could conceivably do that without adventuring if they really wanted to. Instead, if they want to increase certain Traits (Spheres, Abilities, Attributes, Backgrounds, etc.), it should be for a purpose beyond just having them.<br /> <br /> So instead of a character wanting to just become a master Martial Artist (which only requires they max that Trait), have them want to become recognized as a master Martial Artist, which may require fighting significant opponents, winning tournaments, or proving their skill to an authority on the subject (like an ancient master). Rather than a character seeking to create a Wonder for its utility alone, have them desire to make something of lasting value to history, or a Wonder that is important to them and their Paradigm (a Chorister who seeks to forge a literal set of the Armor of God, for example). If a character wants loadsofmoney, ask why the character wants it beyond mere financial security (paying for a loved one's medical bills, settling a debt for honor's sake, leaving behind a sizable inheritance for one's children, etc.).<br /> <br /> Or have their goal be wholly character driven, rather than stat driven. Getting revenge on someone. Convincing one's family that your life choices weren't a mistake (double points if the loved one is also an Enemy because of this ideological disagreement). Finding true love. Getting one's community to accept one's Paradigm, making magick easier while there.<br /> <br /> Having the players come up with long term goals will help them get into the heads of their characters, and think of them as more than just game constructs. Get them invested in their characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T02:09:18-08:00","id":1000669,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, we're about to start the first game on Thursday but I had few things I wanted to ask prior to that. One character took 10 willpower. Is there anything I should prepare for with this? I've ran few vampire games back in the day and recall this was a bit of a nuisance when it came to dominate etc - anything similar here? And if so - any counters?<br /> <br /> Few players ( 2 out of 4 ) picked enemies on 3. I have some ideas but was wondering if you ever had any enemies that I could steal so to say - great ideas, memorable npcs? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Two players have avatar 5 - any advice on how to roleplay this? How significant is this in game - narrative wise.<br /> <br /> More to come I'm afraid...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12551,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","user":"artuard","date":"11-09-2016, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T02:41:09-08:00","id":1000674,"title":"","content":"Willpower: they are going to be ridiculously hard to do mind magic to, and if they ever start astral projecting, they are going to be pretty hardy.<br /> Other than that, they are probably going to e the most caviller when it comes to those automatic successes. So yay.<br /> <br /> Enemies should be matched up with their backstory and should be discussed with the player, the two of you collaborating to make them up. Stock enemies are going to feel much less firing than tailor made enemies.<br /> <br /> Avatar: first things first, what's their Avatar's Essence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T03:29:10-08:00","id":1000691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1000674#post1000674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avatar: first things first, what's their Avatar's Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Primordial and Dynamic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:15:52-08:00","id":1000710,"title":"","content":"Right.<br /> Dynamic avatars are rarely consistent I the way they interact with their mage. They could appear as images, sounds, music, vibrations, feelings, urges, voices, commercials on TV...<br /> However, they are not random, and will probably manifest in ways appropriate in theme to the mage themselves.<br /> Dynamic avatars are agents of change and will constantly push their mage to try and change things up be it ideologically, structurally, or physically, and are almost abstention deficit in their attempts to lead their mage often jumping between several different goals at a time. They get frustrated with mages who try to play it safe and try to stick to the tired and true.<br /> <br /> Primordial avatars tend to be very ancient avatars and may in fact the remnants or fragments of a great and ancient presence. This could be as an angel, a ancient spirit like Gaia, a mythic figure, or even something more general such as the element of fire, an ancient tree, or simply the Hero with 1,000 faces. These avatars are very consistent in how they appear and are often very personal to the mage themselves.<br /> <br /> They are cryptic as hell, and have little patience with mages who don't act how they think they should, and are known to resort to extreme measures to get their point across. Some bully their mage, even threatening them with peril, placing them in life threatening situations until he mage finally gets a clue. They are quite formidable and often force their mage to confront the repetitions that takes place throughout history. Showing how past events can hint ate future ones.<br /> <br /> Without knowing more about the mages in question, I don't dare suggest anything more specific than this. Hope it gives you somewhere to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:46:48-08:00","id":1000722,"title":"","content":"The Revised Storyteller's Handbook has an entire chapter devoted to Avatars and Seekings. I'll be summarizing some relevant points, but I recommend checking it out yourself.<br /> <br /> Avatars, at their core, are forces that are more or less looking out for their Mage's best interest, but have their own plans and goals in mind. They want the Mage to Ascend, but have their own ideas about how to lead them to it. Some might be indirect, dropping clues here and there. Others might be openly helpful, while others antagonistic. The Avatar is ultimately working for the Mage's own good, but the Mage doesn't necessarily see it that way. Work with the players about what sort of relationship they want with their Avatars, both in how they interact and what the Avatars want to teach the characters.<br /> <br /> The Background's rank dictates how heavily the Avatar is involved in the Mage's life, either because of variable power at the Avatar's disposal (a weak Avatar could only do so much), or because of variable investment the Avatar has in the Mage's development (an Avatar could be very powerful, but be very aloof). Regardless, having Avatar 5 means that the characters Avatars are very involved. If they appear in dreams, those dreams will be vivid and frequent. If the Avatar manifests in the flesh, they will make appearances often. These are the sorts of Avatars who show up to talk directly to the Mage, although this is not required.<br /> <br /> Dynamic Avatars are devoted to Change, and will encourage the Mage towards dynamic action. They won't necessarily push them towards a consistent course of action from appearance to appearance, but have the Mage running from cause to cause. Their manifestation won't necessarily be consistent either, though it depends on the player's wishes. They could be any number of different forms but with a persistent trait that identifies them (the color yellow, skulls, fire, etc.). Or take the form of a known revolutionary figure, relevant to the Mage's interests. They will try to prevent the character from becoming complacent, even if that means causing trouble for them.<br /> <br /> Primordial Avatars, by contrast, are three things: Powerful, Mysterious, and <i>Scary</i>. These beings have been around forever, and embody concepts that are very simple in theory, but complicated in execution. A Primoridal Avatar's goals are usually very specific to the theme it represents, and it usually doesn't have much interest in the Mage aside from getting that theme or message across. Even at lower ranks in the Background, these beings aren't weak, so much as less involved; Primordial Avatars represent primal, potent forces, and even a Mage with Avatar 1 can sense this. A fifth rank Primordial Avatar, therefore, is a force of nature and magick that has a very specific purpose, who has decided to give their Mage as close to their undivided attention as Primordial Avatars ever do. In short, the character's encounters with their Avatar will be <i>Intense</i>. Their Avatar might not be their enemy, but they should still be enigmatic and a little frightening.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T06:11:06-08:00","id":1000730,"title":"","content":"I can give you the details no worries: <br /> <br /> First mage, Euthanatos, young girl with amnesia flaw ( I established it has been a severe case of quietus or some paradox backlash ), she has PTSB ( doctors, needles etc ) comming from her imagination that she was experimented on ( which is not true - again that was the paradox - my idea and she doesnt know that ). She is very much into her tradition, has arete 3 and entroy 3 with mind 3. She has wp 10 and a avatar 5 primordial type. Also past lives 3 and arcane 3. 80% of her abilities are combat related. She has a very strong conviction of going after rapists and men who harm women. Her paradigm is that everything is chaos and she draws magic from bits of order ( which is her ultimate goal - order ). Flaw - enemy 3, ptsb and amnesia. No merits<br /> <br /> <br /> Second mage : Hermetic mage, young guy - friend of the girl above, weak will wp5, addicted to drugs but well off resources 5 and matter and forces with prime to enhance drugs, hedonist, oportunist with dynamic avatar rating 5, patron 3 and flaws: addiction, curse, gambler and enemy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> CHRIST.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T06:42:47-08:00","id":1000751,"title":"","content":"As mentioned above the biggest thing Willpower 10 means is that the Mage in question is going to be very difficult to nearly impossible to use mind control on, as well as often having Willpower to spend.<br /> <br /> As for Avatar 5 some thoughts, first if they have 5 points there it means they are likely lacking in other spots. While Im not advocating ruthlessly going after background deficiencies I am suggesting not letting them get a free ride one to pay attention to is Node. Having Avatar 5 and being able to spend 5 quintessence a turn is great and all, but is of lesser value when you dont have an easier way of replenishing that. Also I dont see Chantry or Sanctum which means the Mages in question dont have any place where their effects are going to be safely coincidental (barring a few exceptions).<br /> <br /> As for what it means regarding the Mage/Avatar relationship, I point to the lines from M20 pg 266 <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The stronger the Avatar, the greater its influence; one or two dots in Avatar manifest as simple hunches, whereas four- or five dot ones achieve full-blown identities. </div> </div> </div>A four or five dot Avatar should feel like a separate entity in many ways, often seeming like it has its own desires and goals (even if such things really are taken with the Mage's best interests in mind) and trying to push the Mage toward those desires. <br /> <br /> M20 pg 338 <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Part of the Avatar\u2019s role involves challenge; without challenges, after all, we don\u2019t grow. And so, even the most subtle, agreeable Genius will nag your mage toward new accomplishments and potential failures. A truly strong Avatar (one rated at 4 or 5) can be a terror \u2013 a literal demon, perhaps, that drives the mage night and day. Your mage\u2019s Essence determines the sort of challenges it gives you. A Dynamic spirit ignites passions, a Static one demands perfection, a Questing one tugs you to pursue new avenues of experience, and a Primal one presents constant enigmas and puzzles that apparently defy solutions. In many ways, the Avatar is an internal mentor\u2026 one that never goes away. </div> </div> </div>While I'm not saying nag them until they hate having taken the background, do have their Avatars being more vocal than other characters. These potent Avatars will try to push the Mage toward certain actions and deeds.<br /> <br /> M20 pg 267 <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dynamic - In more subtle forms, this Essence inspires curiosity, impatience, and sudden flashes of brilliance. Appearing in the form of shadows, whispers, and poor impulse control, it goads a mage to treat every day like an adventure. At higher levels, a Dynamic Avatar can nag a person mercilessly, leaving half-finished projects and shattered relationships in the wake of a mage who rarely sits still for long. </div> </div> </div>Dynamic Avatars want their Mages to be agents of change and to have them take action in the world. Carpe Diem could very easily be a catch phrase of the Dynamic essence. The Dynamic Avatar wants to squeeze the opportunity out of every moment right now. Indolence, sloth, and procrastination are things that will get the Dynamic Avatar up in arms and shouting in the Mage's head.<ul><li>Considering the Hermetics background and flaws their Avatar probably comes across like a frat brother or drinking buddy pushing the Mage to enjoy to live each day like its their last. While the Avatar doesnt want to hurt the Mage through their addiction it does feed on the live everyday to the fullest mindset the drugs and gambling represent. Conversely this could mean the Avatar occasionally steers the Mage away from their flaws, especially if it would lead to great danger; after all there are no more moments to seize if the Mage is dead or severely injured but instead of saying no the Avatar is likely to push the Mage to a different action (essentially the Avatar will occasionally be the good friend who takes the keys and makes sure their buddy gets home safe so they can party tomorrow).</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Primordial - A Primordial mage loves mystery. Like deep water, she seeps into hidden places and defies easy understanding. Whereas Pattern people are bricks or stone, Primordial folks are riptides and dark pools. The few Technocrats who favor this Essence understand that no science can penetrate the richest mysteries of the universe; they\u2019ll give lip service to technology, but they always keep a few extra cards up their sleeves for the time when the light fails and order becomes a punch line in the cosmic jest. </div> </div> </div>Primordial Avatars are often some of the most difficult to portray. Generally I view Primordial Avatars appearing various ways, as Lovecraftian entities representing the ancient chaos of the universe, old gods and mythological and religious figures representative of the old ways, or ancestor spirits a direct link to the Mage's past. These Avatars can come across as dark, eerie, sinister, and seductive and influence the Mage to a similar leaning. The Primordial Avatar will push the Mage to remember the old ways and not rely on technology or modern tricks, but rather in their own skills. The Primordial Avatar cautions secrecy and that the Mage should always have a backup plan and offers hidden depths of wisdom and the occasional bit of sagely advice. Essentially Primordial Avatars are Batman without the gadgets - dark, mysterious, with long running plans and gambits that others cant easily uncover but they have the Mage's best interests in mind. Being foolishly open about oneself and relying on technology and new gadgets (not saying dont use them, but not make them the sole basis of their attempt) will have the dark thing expressing its displeasure.<ul><li>Considering the characters Past Lives this means the Avatar is likely to appear as a combination of death related entities (Grim Reaper, Ghosts, Hades) or ancestors of the character. While she might not remember what happened to her, an interesting twist could be the Avatar does know but doesnt say (remember secretive) rather taking advantage of the amnesia to push the Mage to achievements that she would have resisted before (the whole she wants order vs Primordial often representing chaos). At the same time the Avatar will influence the style of order as it represents an ancient chaotic state so any order it would support are going to be modeled after the old ways and respect for those who came before.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Enemies is often times a boon to the Storyteller. It gives you a pre-determined foe which can help get plots moving or prod the character to action if they remain staid for too long. The Enemy should be tied to the character and background and at 3 points is going to be superior to the starting Mage; so what did the Mage do to earn the ire of this person or group? An enemy should be more than Technocrats hate the Traditions as Reality Deviants or similar stereotypes; the hatred and loathing from Enemy comes from a personal place, the enemy doesnt hate them because of what group they align with they hate the Mage.<ul><li>Death of a partner, loved one, close friend: The Ascension War is a war and its often bloody and the death of someone close can lead to a lifelong hatred. For inspiration &quot;My name is Inigo Montoya, you killed my father, prepare to die.&quot; Could work with either character, amnesia makes it easy for all sorts of things to come up and someone into the drug scene especially with money has all sorts of chances to end up purposefully or accidentally getting someone killed (overdose, drug deal gone bad, etc).</li> <li>They should have been mine: The Mage in question was being pursued and courted by the enemy and the Mage spurned them (this does not have to be romantic, think Star Wars &quot;He will join us or die.&quot;) The enemy takes the logic that if they cant have them no one can to its logical end. Considering the Hermetic's addiction perhaps a Nephandi was subtly providing drugs and maneuvering to place the Mage under their sway, but the Mage caught on (perhaps through that Avatar) that something was amiss and turned the Mage away.</li> <li>Betrayal: At one point in happier times the Mage and the enemy were friends or at least close allies. Something happened and they turned on each other and the enemy has taken that sense of betrayal to heart. More likely for the Hermetic as drug use can make people do things they regret later.</li> <li>Legacy Hatred: The enemy wanted someone else dead and they had the temerity to die through someone else's hand. Denied their vengeance they decided to go for the next of kin in a sort of macabre inheritance. To their anger this new foe is as recalcitrant to die as their former one and it fuels their hate further. One of the few exceptions to hating the Mage, rather the hatred is displaced from the one that denied them vengeance to their next of kin. Could work well with the girl due to the Past Lives, perhaps the most recent Past Life was the enemy's former foe.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:06:58-08:00","id":1000826,"title":"","content":"This is phenomenal guys. Quick follow up - if I decide to create actual people speaking to the players as avatars - would other players see them as well? Or would they require spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:12:00-08:00","id":1000830,"title":"","content":"The Enemies should be worked out with the players, though I can give further suggestions.<ul><li>The Enemy's actions don't necessarily need to be directed at killing the Mage. They could decide they'd rather humiliate or ruin the character, as it could be more satisfying (and safer for the Enemy, if directly attacking the Mage would lead to other problems). Opposition can take many forms, which can keep the PCs on their toes.</li> <li>The Enemy doesn't even need to actually hate the Mage in question. Perhaps their interests are simply opposed, and the Enemy sees their conflict as a brutal necessity. The Enemy might admire the Mage, respect them - even love them. Consider an Enemy who believes they oppose the Mage for their own good. Or the Enemy is messed up in the head, and attacking the Mage is considered an expression of their positive emotions. Maybe the Enemy is a former family member who radically disagrees with the Mage's lifestyle, and is working to push them out of it.</li> <li>The Enemy could, in some way, be a reflection of the Mage. Some aspect of their character - their beliefs, their skill set, their attitude, their background - is reminiscent of the Mage. They could be the Mage if their beliefs or methods were taken to their logical extreme...or, alternatively, that the Mage is the one whose beliefs are corrupted forms of their adversary. It lends a poetic edge to the conflict, as the Mage is forced to look in the mirror darkly (or lightly).</li> <li>The Mage's Enemy <i>is also their Avatar</i>. Consider my above point about an Enemy acting in opposition to the Mage for what they perceive is the Mage's own good. Now consider that the Enemy is right, because they are the Mage's Avatar. Avatars can appear in many guises, and many Mages don't recognize their Avatars for what they are. It's possible that the Mage finds herself opposed by an implacable adversary, who seems to know the Mage intimately, has no recognizable motive besides giving the Mage a hard time, and, worst of all, <i>wields magick without suffering Paradox</i>. (Because, for reasons unknown, Avatars are not affected by Paradox). It's a frightening Enemy to be sure, and one tailor made to galvanize the Mage to action.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:18:39-08:00","id":1000833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1000826#post1000826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is phenomenal guys. Quick follow up - if I decide to create actual people speaking to the players as avatars - would other players see them as well? Or would they require spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could go either way, really. The Avatar could manifest physically, so anyone could see them normally. Or they could be a vision only the Mage could see, which may or may not be noticeable by other characters with Spirit or Mind. It depends on whether you want the entire Cabal to get involved with a given character's personal Avatar business.<br /> <br /> Although, if you take my advice above about the Avatar acting as an adversary, it might help to keep the true nature of the being a mystery if everyone can see it (at least, when the Avatar wants to be seen). Then again, an Avatar Enemy doesn't need to get personally involved for them to act in opposition to the Mage. They could arrange actions against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T10:47:29-08:00","id":1000880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1000826#post1000826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is phenomenal guys. Quick follow up - if I decide to create actual people speaking to the players as avatars - would other players see them as well? Or would they require spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I would keep them visible only to the character unless someone else is using Spirit and Mind since the Avatar while a powerful entity is still very much a part of the Mage.<br /> <br /> If these are newer players I would steer away from making the Avatar the enemy simply because it can lead to confusion and fights and it could feel like you are being punitive for them taking Avatar 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:05:57-08:00","id":1000890,"title":"","content":"One last thing I'd add.<br /> Ask your players something like &quot;how does your Mages avatar appear to your Mage, and how aware are they of them?&quot;<br /> <br /> Do they think the avatar is a part of their subconcious? An aspect of a greater spirit? A personified manifestation of the Mages will? An alien presence? The reincarnated soul of a Mage of the past? Just a trick of the mind?<br /> <br /> Obviously at Avatar 5 it's going to be impossible to be oblivious of them, but perhaps they'll still be uncertain how much of their avatar is them vs other.<br /> <br /> Sit will be something for the player and you to develop together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:12:52-08:00","id":1000895,"title":"","content":"I was playing with the idea that they would never know that it's their avatar - hence a visible for everyone person, mysteriously showing up from time - absolutely not an enemy, But Not sure it's not counter intuitive to the concept of avatar itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:36:21-08:00","id":1000911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1000890#post1000890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One last thing I'd add.<br /> Ask your players something like &quot;how does your Mages avatar appear to your Mage, and how aware are they of them?&quot;<br /> <br /> Do they think the avatar is a part of their subconcious? An aspect of a greater spirit? A personified manifestation of the Mages will? An alien presence? The reincarnated soul of a Mage of the past? Just a trick of the mind?<br /> <br /> Obviously at Avatar 5 it's going to be impossible to be oblivious of them, but perhaps they'll still be uncertain how much of their avatar is them vs other.<br /> <br /> Sit will be something for the player and you to develop together.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Initially I wanted to - but keep in mind that they're seriously overloaded with the whole paradigm stuff from before - I felt like adding more to their character creation would eventually do more harm than good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T13:26:58-08:00","id":1000959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1000895#post1000895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was playing with the idea that they would never know that it's their avatar - hence a visible for everyone person, mysteriously showing up from time - absolutely not an enemy, But Not sure it's not counter intuitive to the concept of avatar itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>The description of the Avatar background implies only the Mage can normally perceive it M20 pg 305 <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This Trait measures your Awakened self, reflects its ability to shift and hold Quintessence, and determines how real it is in your character\u2019s perceptions. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:21:27-08:00","id":1001246,"title":"","content":"Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:47:08-08:00","id":1001255,"title":"","content":"Speaking of quintessence - quick one: How can they replenish that if they have limited backgrounds ( like avatar 5 but no nodes etc ). I know prime 3 starts to open some forms of leaching quintessence from objects and later on from forces and life. But does it recharge at a slow rate automatically? I couldn't find it yet in the book - I'm trying to find it atm but huh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:54:00-08:00","id":1001260,"title":"","content":"Prime gives you quint:<br /> At 1 in exchange for HL<br /> At 3 leeching from mages, tass and distant nodes(correspondence 3 required), sacrifices are also a possibility now.<br /> At 4 you can unweave patterns(living ones exempt) and use the quint from it.<br /> At 5 you can unweave lifeforms and use the quint from it. You can create new nodes and get quint everywhere (from the universal pool or however your Paradigm calls it)<br /> <br /> So without access to a node they must steal it or burn valuable things or they demand payment in quint/trade something for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":".  Clarification 11-10-2016, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T02:08:30-08:00","id":1001263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1001260#post1001260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime gives you quint:<br /> At 1 in exchange for HL<br /> At 3 leeching from mages, tass and distant nodes(correspondence 3 required), sacrifices are also a possibility now.<br /> At 4 you can unweave patterns(living ones exempt) and use the quint from it.<br /> At 5 you can unweave lifeforms and use the quint from it. You can create new nodes and get quint everywhere (from the universal pool or however your Paradigm calls it)<br /> <br /> So without access to a node they must steal it or burn valuable things or they demand payment in quint/trade something for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sorry for being noobish but what does HL stand for? How do they 'steal' it ( I assume thats without prime? )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12551,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","user":"artuard","date":". 11-10-2016, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T02:48:29-08:00","id":1001275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1001263#post1001263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry for being noobish but what does HL stand for? How do they 'steal' it ( I assume thats without prime? )</div> </div> </div> </div>Heath Levels. Basically it allows you to sacrifice damage for Quint, at one HL a pop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T02:50:49-08:00","id":1001277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1001275#post1001275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heath Levels. Basically it allows you to sacrifice damage for Quint, at one HL a pop.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh and any mage can do that? No prime required and aggravated damage I presume?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T03:22:25-08:00","id":1001284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1001277#post1001277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh and any mage can do that? No prime required and aggravated damage I presume?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well no, you need Prime 1. And yes, Aggravated. In fact, it's a special kind of Aggravated that can't be healed with Magick. Only time and rest (and medical attention, presumably) can repair pattern damage of this level. For this reason, most Mages only use their Bruised Health Level. Unless you're prepared to get your Martyr on, like the Choristers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T04:00:36-08:00","id":1001293,"title":"","content":"Well this will be fun :-) I shall take advantage of that haha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T11:25:56-08:00","id":1001405,"title":"","content":"Woith stealing I meant Tass, Node raiding and Periapts. Plus you can steal Quint from another mage (if he has more quint than Avatar)<br /> To get the quint out of someone/something and into your own pattern you need Prime at 3.<br /> <br /> To just use it, you have to hold the periapt or the tass or use Prime 2 (with added Correspondence 2 if the target is not in clear sensory range)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T08:49:24-08:00","id":1003423,"title":"","content":"Our first game was a blast! All four players were amazed at the range of options their respective characters have with spheres, up top the point where they would spend long minutes trying to 'open unlocked door' haha<br /> As a side note I must confess that I overloaded them with supernatural events up to the point where I had to moderate myself - all four avatars were manifesting themselves causing confusion and uncertainty, one player had a curse flaw that triggered, the main plot was evolving when players decided to search for backup among other supernatural entities - from Vampires to bargaining a pact with a Demon. Seriously I had to take notes quite early on just to make sure I don't forget it all.<br /> <br /> I think, that for the next game I will limit the avatar manifestations and focus a bit more on the actual plot for a change. The game is quite hard to control with so many variables in play!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12551,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","user":"artuard","date":".  spelling 11-15-2016, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T13:46:02-08:00","id":1003578,"title":"","content":"Awesome to hear!<br /> Yeah, note taking is essential. Always write down at least the key bullet points of plot and npc relations that occur.<br /> I'd say don't worry about keeping track of active effects across sessions, just ask the players to keep traj of their effects and ask at the start of each session if they currently have any ongoing magic.<br /> <br /> Similarly, it's their job to keep track of their flaws as much as you, so make that clear for a role playing standpoint that it matters.<br /> <br /> Sounds as though you've got things pretty much under control though. One thing you could do is, now you've hit them with a load if supernatural, is to through a dash of the mundane at them. Have them deal with landlords, police, maybe a nosey neighbour or two. Havering sleepers come up can be a really good balance for be more fantastic elements, as well as give the players a real feeling of power. That and it also forces the players to watch their vulgar effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T15:53:06-08:00","id":1003650,"title":"","content":"It's probably a good idea to focus on the Plot for a little while. Once they've advanced it a bit, you can take a break and let them attend to subplots and character interactions. I don't know if your Plot is one of those that has everything happen in a short period of in-game time, but I would recommend giving the characters downtime between major story beats. Many situations occur over days, weeks, or months. While this cuts into the sense of urgency of the Plot, it also gives your characters breathing room and a chance to better themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T23:51:23-08:00","id":1003800,"title":"","content":"I gave them a time frame of 30 days to do something - it's not a hard deadline - they just have to obtain an item from a location in that time, up to them how and if at all - there will be some consequences if they do it or don't, that's it. So there is a lot of time to do all sorts of stuff in between.<br /> But yeah, I plan to hit them with mundane now haha - this is a great idea - already have several ideas. One player is a kid ( flaw child ) so his my idea is that his parents plan to move away from NY where the chronicle is taking place - if he want's to stay he has to convince them somehow that it is better to stay. And the other players GF will be pregnant soon ;-) that should shake it up a bit.<br /> <br /> I also realized I made a few minor mistakes, sadly. The kid has 8 spheres at 1, with arete 1. However it looks like I allowed him to use an effect from correspondence 2 ( he opened a window to look at distance ). Have to backtrack that option .., and I forgot using tools lowers the arete difficulty :-/ They failed a few simple effects that could have otherwise been successful because of this. I have to prepare more paperwork .<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T01:22:24-08:00","id":1003819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1001284#post1001284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well no, you need Prime 1. And yes, Aggravated. In fact, it's a special kind of Aggravated that can't be healed with Magick. Only time and rest (and medical attention, presumably) can repair pattern damage of this level. For this reason, most Mages only use their Bruised Health Level. Unless you're prepared to get your Martyr on, like the Choristers.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Verbena get their enhanced variant of Heart's Blood in their Tradbook, where they can get 1 Quint for 1 (non-Magickally healable only) bashing damage instead, and 2 for the usual nasty variant. Kind of super powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T08:58:11-08:00","id":1003965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1001284#post1001284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well no, you need Prime 1. And yes, Aggravated. In fact, it's a special kind of Aggravated that can't be healed with Magick. Only time and rest (and medical attention, presumably) can repair pattern damage of this level. For this reason, most Mages only use their Bruised Health Level. Unless you're prepared to get your Martyr on, like the Choristers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be wrong, but it is not possible to heal the damage with quint? Without an effect even?<br /> It sounds logical, but could be a HR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T14:43:46-08:00","id":1004119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1003965#post1003965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may be wrong, but it is not possible to heal the damage with quint? Without an effect even?<br /> It sounds logical, but could be a HR.</div> </div> </div> </div>I checked both Mage Revised and How Do You Do That?, and both state quite clearly that Heart's Blood cannot be healed with magick, only with time and rest.<br /> <br /> Strangely, neither source actually specifies what <i>kind</i> of damage is taken when a Mage does this. I was just assuming it was Aggravated. That said, Prime damage is usually Aggravated - it damages the Pattern, after all - so it's fair to assume that Heart's Blood does it as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T01:59:37-08:00","id":1004297,"title":"","content":"Actually, it seems there is one more thing I need explaining. Resonance. Is it just a narrative thing in your games? Like a touch/vibe of ones personal magic that manifests once per game or so? Does it only relate to PCs? How would you guys explain this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T05:04:40-08:00","id":1004339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1004297#post1004297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it seems there is one more thing I need explaining. Resonance. Is it just a narrative thing in your games? Like a touch/vibe of ones personal magic that manifests once per game or so? Does it only relate to PCs? How would you guys explain this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the single most confounding &quot;stat&quot; in the game. To put it plainly, resonance is more a roleplay thing that it is something to level up, a way of both individualising how your mage does magic as well as a way of reflecting the kinds of maic your mage tends to perform.<br /> <br /> At te start of the game the players chose a resonance type and descriptor, like static rhythmic, or entropic burning.<br /> Story wise this defines the kind of way ther magic manifests, so if you have a burning resonance, your invisibility effect may take the form if burning light away, while rhythmic resonance would push light away via alternating pulses at similar frequency. It's more it flavour than anything else.<br /> <br /> Gameplay wise, magic is easier if doing an effect which fits their resonance, so doing fire magic to burn things is helped by a burning resonance. However if you wanted to quench a fire, you might be going against your resonance and is thus harder.<br /> <br /> Another use for resonance is as an identifier for effects. If your arch enemy has a dynamic morphing entropic melting resonance, you'd be able to sense that in their effects. A perception+awareness roll would be enough to pick his up and remind you who was here.<br /> For less familiar resonances, Mind 1 would be enough to detect any resonance in the area, and can help in detective work for identifying mages responsible for doing certain things.<br /> <br /> Finally, you can use resonance as a way of consequence for particularly brutal or outlandish uses of magic.<br /> If you do a big effect to kill a lot of people, you may get some nasty entropic resonance, similarly if you solidify or encase something or do something particularly chaotic. You'll have to make a judgement call on what is deserving of a change in resonance.<br /> <br /> More points in a resonance does not provide any real benefit, it just means your resonance is stronger, and may manifest is subtle ways. A strong entropic burning resonance may manifest in having what ever the mage holds becoming ever so slightly singed, or a small ploom of steam emanating from them. While Static Rhythmic might manifest in their movement being somewhat unnaturally well timed, as though they can't help but move to a hidden beat.<br /> <br /> This is also a fun tool for NPC description.<br /> <br /> Optionally, you can have anyone in excess of 5 points of resonance suseptible to falling into Quiet.<br /> Another fun rule is having a mages resonance cause certain other mages with opposing resonances act somewhat auspiciously, or with matching resonances to have some kind of synergy.<br /> <br /> It's up to you though how big a role resonance plays in your game.<br /> <br /> I tend to hange my players resonance depending on the kind of magic they do, keeping an almost arbitrary tally of entropic, dynamic, and static type effects, and throwing an extra dot into one of them one every 8 or so sessions.<br /> However, on the whole, resonance change is best reserved for big life changing events like seekings, Herculean tasks, or moral peril.<br /> <br /> You'll know when it'll be appropriate.<br /> <br /> Pay close attention to your Euthanatos mage, they are especially susceptible to getting entropic resonance by killing excessively. Jhor is the name for that kind of resonance and if any Euthanatos discovers one of their own with too much Jhor, then it may be time to deal with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 11-17-2016, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T07:15:50-08:00","id":1004395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1004339#post1004339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Welcome to the single most confounding &quot;stat&quot; in the game. To put it plainly, resonance is more a roleplay thing that it is something to level up, a way of both individualising how your mage does magic as well as a way of reflecting the kinds of maic your mage tends to perform.<br /> <br /> At te start of the game the players chose a resonance type and descriptor, like static rhythmic, or entropic burning.<br /> Story wise this defines the kind of way ther magic manifests, so if you have a burning resonance, your invisibility effect may take the form if burning light away, while rhythmic resonance would push light away via alternating pulses at similar frequency. It's more it flavour than anything else.<br /> <br /> Gameplay wise, magic is easier if doing an effect which fits their resonance, so doing fire magic to burn things is helped by a burning resonance. However if you wanted to quench a fire, you might be going against your resonance and is thus harder.<br /> <br /> Another use for resonance is as an identifier for effects. If your arch enemy has a dynamic morphing entropic melting resonance, you'd be able to sense that in their effects. A perception+awareness roll would be enough to pick his up and remind you who was here.<br /> For less familiar resonances, Mind 1 would be enough to detect any resonance in the area, and can help in detective work for identifying mages responsible for doing certain things.<br /> <br /> Finally, you can use resonance as a way of consequence for particularly brutal or outlandish uses of magic.<br /> If you do a big effect to kill a lot of people, you may get some nasty entropic resonance, similarly if you solidify or encase something or do something particularly chaotic. You'll have to make a judgement call on what is deserving of a change in resonance.<br /> <br /> More points in a resonance does not provide any real benefit, it just means your resonance is stronger, and may manifest is subtle ways. A strong entropic burning resonance may manifest in having what ever the mage holds becoming ever so slightly singed, or a small ploom of steam eminating from them. While Static Rhythmic might manifest in their movement being somewhat unnaturally well timed, as though they can't help but move to a hidden beat.<br /> <br /> This is also a fun tool for NPC description.<br /> <br /> Optionally, you can have anyone in excess of 5 points of resonance suseptible to falling into Quiet.<br /> Another fun rule is having a mages resonance cause certain other mages with opposing resonances act somewhat ausspeciously, or with matching resonances to have some kind of synergy.<br /> <br /> It's up to you though how big a roll resonance plays in your game.<br /> <br /> I tend to hange my players resonance depending on the kind of magic they do, keeping an almost arbitrary tally of entropic, dynamic, and static type effects, and throwing an extra dot into one of them one every 8 or so sessions.<br /> However, on the whole, resonance change is best reserved for big life changing events like seekings, Herculean tasks, or moral peril.<br /> <br /> You'll know when it'll be appropriate.<br /> <br /> Pay close attention to your Euthanatos mage, they are especially auseptable to getting entropic resonance by killing excessively. Jhor is the name for that kind of resonance and if any Euthanatos discovers one of their own with too much Jhor, then it may be time to deal with them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a><br /> <br /> I think I will change this a bit to suit my Chronicle - There is just enough happening at the moment for me to keep tracking one more trait. So I will make it narrative at the moment, so they will only know what sort of resonance they have by description. I like the Jhor aspect - will keep that in mind. Much obliged Sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T08:34:35-08:00","id":1004442,"title":"","content":"Quick follow up question: what is this purple paradigm everyone is talking about? :x","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T10:08:35-08:00","id":1004500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1004442#post1004442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick follow up question: what is this purple paradigm everyone is talking about? :x</div> </div> </div> </div>Purple Paradigm is the term for discussing if Mages realized they were working their will and dont need the various paradigms, instruments, and practices; essentially as if they had read the Mage the Ascension rulebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","user":"Cynic01","date":". 11-17-2016, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T13:18:28-08:00","id":1004596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynic01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1004500#post1004500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Purple Paradigm is the term for discussing if Mages realized they were working their will and dont need the various paradigms, instruments, and practices; essentially as if they had read the Mage the Ascension rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's for this reason that a lot of new players argue about ditching the Focus system and letting characters do whatever they want. These new players mistake what's written in the rulebook for common knowledge in-universe. In truth, Mages either have never heard of this idea, or scoff at it. At best, the Traditions and other Crafts pay lip service to the idea of pure will-working, for the sake of political expediency. Everyone thinks their Paradigm is correct...and, despite the mechanics and the rulebook, they can't be proven wrong. Most Traditions have their own reasons for why a particularly accomplished Mage is capable of doing magick without Instruments. Reasons that only reinforce their Paradigms. Certain groups - the Order of Hermes and Yoga-using Euthanatoi - even make it a state to aspire to, having ceased to use magick, and instead become it, while still working within the same metaphysical framework.<br /> <br /> The way previous Editions read, it presented individual Mage Paradigms as hindrances to their development. As the game went on, it became more and more about maintaining that, even if a Mage doesn't need their Instruments, that doesn't mean they have to abandon all of their beliefs.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think that's good. Players shouldn't think of their character's beliefs as impediments to enjoying the game. They should think of them as chances to roleplay and create good stories, especially if the world view they roleplay is vastly different from what the player may believe in real life. Or, alternatively, allowing the player to put their personal beliefs into practice in ways they never could in Real Life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T04:42:24-08:00","id":1005303,"title":"","content":"I see, thank You!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:52:49-08:00","id":1011203,"title":"","content":"Hi Guys, back again :-) Was wondering if Any of you Gents would have mage 20th cheat sheets - printable resources that seem to be absolutely crucial for a game. <br /> Any links would be appriciated :-) <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T14:12:41-08:00","id":1011216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1011203#post1011203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Guys, back again :-) Was wondering if Any of you Gents would have mage 20th cheat sheets - printable resources that seem to be absolutely crucial for a game. <br /> Any links would be appriciated :-) <br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of things do you need to consult exactly?<br /> <br /> If you have the PDF, them you could just print out the pages with the tables on them, and use those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:23:26-08:00","id":1011242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1011216#post1011216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of things do you need to consult exactly?<br /> <br /> If you have the PDF, them you could just print out the pages with the tables on them, and use those.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aye, I have the PDF file - so far I've printed out 501-510 from your post earlier in this thread - was wondering if I'm missing any more critical info that I should prepare?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:32:34-08:00","id":1011250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1011242#post1011242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Aye, I have the PDF file - so far I've printed out 501-510 from your post earlier in this thread - was wondering if I'm missing any more critical info that I should prepare?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends entirely on what you feel is lacking.<br /> What do you need?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T15:56:34-08:00","id":1011258,"title":"","content":"Ah well it's hard to say like that, but I know I lack knowledge in the Umbra ( one player has spirit 3 ), magical items and I guess combat wouldn't hurt either?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T17:10:05-08:00","id":1011279,"title":"","content":"Oh boy... You've picked a pretty large couple of subjects there.<br /> <br /> Combat: Take a look at page 445 onwards for all the combat tables. There are a lot of them, so take a look at the ones you think are relevant to you and print them out. You might even want to copy and paste some of these tables onto another sheet of paper to cut down on how much you need to print. But they'll provide more than what you'll ever need.<br /> My personal opinion is these tables are overkill. If you need this many tables to run a game, then perhaps the rules are starting to get in the way of the story. But to each their own.<br /> <br /> Now, the Umbra is its own special little headache. Page 85 onwards of M20 gives a pretty good almost all encompassing guide to the Other Worlds, though I'm guessing you already read it and found it lacking.<br /> <br /> The books that detail the Umbra specifically are:<br /> <br /> Book of Worlds :- reads like a travel guide written by Mages, and can be a bit obnoxious at times, though there's a good list of systems and rules on the back pages, if somewhat incomplete. It goes through everything, the Three Worlds, the Dreamlands, Paradox Realms, Horizon and Deep umbra locals. Though it's 2nd ed, so no storm, and Diossetep is still in tact. This book goes through how sphere magic is affected by the various realms, as well as how paradox may manifest on each.<br /> <br /> Infinite Tapestry :- reads like a cross between a spiritual enlightenment guide, and a textbook on astrophysics. If you're getting into this one, be prepared for a lot of thinking. It deals with the Spirit world post Reckoning, and adds a few new features such as Disembodiment, as well as a few tricks to get around the Avatar Storm such as Astral Sojourn. This book does NOT look at the Middle or the Dark umbra at all, but instead focuses in incredible detail on the Astral Umbra. The book will also talk about Horizon and the Deep umbra, but it seems to me as though it's written under the assumption that you've already read Book of Worlds, make references to locations described in greater detail there.<br /> <br /> Other than that, you'll have to go to different game lines for more details.<br /> <br /> WTA: Umbra :- This goes into detail on the Middle Umbra, also known as the Spirit Wilds. While Book of Worlds details the realms of the Middle Umbra adequately and tells you all the Mage relevant parts, the Werewolf book goes into much greater detail, and has a lot more information on the Penumbra than any other book I've read before it. Bare in mind that this is a Werewolf book, so it won't give you any information on Sphere magic or Paradox, and some of the realms aren't really accessible to Mages normally (like Wolfhome or Pangea). But there's more than enough in there to warrant giving it a quick look.<br /> <br /> W20 Umbra: The Velvet Shadow :- This one is much like the other Umbra book in terms of focus, Middle Umbra and Penumbra stuff abound, but it goes a lot deeper and more detailed than its predecessor. It even has details on the Astral Realm and the Deep Umbra, though not much. Again, it's a Werewolf book, so nothing on magic, though plenty of Spirits if that's your thing. Formatting isn't nearly as tight as it is in Umbra though.<br /> <br /> WTA: Rage Across The Heavens :- This gives you the Werewolf take on Horizon and the Deep Umbra (a distinction that Werewolf doesn't actually make). It serves as an alternative route through the planets that only Mystic Mages would have access to. Again it's written for Werewolf games, so all it can offer you is ideas. Not as useful as others, but still a fun read. Loads of information on spirits and Umbral Navigation though.<br /> <br /> Wraith 2nd Ed :- This one is essential if you're planning trips into the Dark Umbra. The first 3 or 4 chapters are dedicated to explaining the Shadowlands and the Tempest well enough to start. Every expansion will add a bit more to the realm of the dead, whether it's the Shadowland citadels, Stygia, the Yellow Springs, or the Labyrinth that tickles your fancy, there's a book on it somewhere (or not, Wraith was discontinued prematurely, but oh well). Most Mages never see the Dark Umbra, though it could be worth looking into for your Euthanatos. Also gives a deeper context to why they see the Good Death as an important rite, it prevents humans becoming Wraiths.<br /> <br /> Changeling: The Dreaming 2nd :- If you you want to deal with the Maya, also called the Dreaming, then Changeling will give you a wealth of inspiration to draw from. The Dreaming is the least static of all of the other worlds, so you can get away with making a lot more stuff up and having it be just as good as canon. The only Mages who can voluntarily explore the Dreaming is, unsurprisingly, the Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, that should give you an idea on just how vast the topic of the Umbra is if you look at everything. So I'm going to ask a few questions to help narrow it down for you.<br /> <br /> Is the Avatar Storm in your game?<br /> <br /> What kind of mage is your Spirit 3 guy?<br /> <br /> What kind of Chronicle are you running? (Themes, plot, setting, etc...)<br /> <br /> Do you use spirits in your game, and if so what kind?<br /> <br /> Do you want to set whole stories in the Umbra for a while?<br /> <br /> Are you happy with your mages going to space? (It was all the rage back in 2nd ed)<br /> <br /> <br /> One more thing. Not too long ago I made a post on this forum trying to put the various levels of the Spirit World in order. Not sure if it will be of use to you, but it's something which seemed relevant to mention.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy\"> A Mage's Guide to the Galaxy - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1005413-a-mage-s-guide-to-the-galaxy </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Been reading over Book of Worlds and Infinite Tapestry and just wanted to try and get this all straight in my head. First of all, bellow is my understanding of the basic set up of Spiritual Cosmology Mundane Earth ==GAUNTLET== Penumbra -Astral Videre -Videre Spiritum (WtA penumbra) -Videre Mortus (WtO shadowlands) - The Dreaming (CtD &amp;quot;penumbra&amp;quot;) Near Umbra -High Umbra -- Vulgate, Afterworlds, Spires, Courts, Epiphamies, etc. Middle Umbra -- all the various realms such as Flux, Scar, the Aetherial Realm, the Abyss, etc. -- many zones such as mirror zones, null zones, and vistas, the </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-02-2016, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T18:50:13-08:00","id":1011303,"title":"","content":"Okay, Magical Items...<br /> <br /> The <i>Revised Storyteller's Companion</i> (not the Handbook) has a chapter on Wonders. The material there is fairly useful, and includes a few Rotes adding onto it (like how Matter 3 can be used to make an object resistant to most mundane damage, something the Sphere description never really touches upon).<br /> <br /> But the most important source on magical items is <i>Forged By Dragon's Fire</i>, an entire book devoted to the subject. It expands on some (but not all) of the material from the above book, as well as giving new stuff (like Grimoires and Primers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T19:01:52-08:00","id":1011304,"title":"","content":"Ok - First of all Thank YOU :-) <br /> <br /> Now - I got the combat ( 10 pages ) and casting magick ( 10 pages ) printed out, will throw out those that seem overkill later on. <br /> <br /> Also, Holy crap! I expected Umbra to be complicated but this is just crazy. I will stick to mage 20th info and your link guide to galaxy as that's exactly what I was looking for - a quick look at how this is built. <br /> <br /> your questions- <br /> <br /> 1) Yes, I want the avatar storm - mainly as a form of delay before the spirit guy hacks his way through the gauntlet. <br /> <br /> 2) Spirit guy is a Verbena modern shaman ( ER doctor in his mundane life ) with strong life ( 3) and spirit ( 3 ) and basic prime ( 1 ) . He has celtic/irish roots and that's his paradigm as well - a modern druid so to speak. He is curious about the spirit world but wants to take thing slow about it. <br /> <br /> 3) My chronicle is based in NY - It will be focused in this city at least for few months before they choose to do something else. <br /> <br /> 4) I haven't used spirits yet, but I want to yes - I wanted to introduce the city father and the chronicle will touch the egiptian spirits ( They're trying to steal/obtain an ancient egiptian artifact ). <br /> <br /> 5) Not for the time being as I'm not confident about Umbra at all - if anything your post freaked me out even more haha<br /> <br /> 6) Doubt they would want to do that - but hey - if they do I would rather be prepared.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T19:09:36-08:00","id":1011306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1011303#post1011303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the most important source on magical items is <i>Forged By Dragon's Fire</i>, an entire book devoted to the subject. It expands on some (but not all) of the material from the above book, as well as giving new stuff (like Grimoires and Primers).</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing to be aware of here. Prime levels used for making Magic Items work differently in M20 than it does in rev ed's FBDF.<br /> <br /> Personally I prefer Revised, but if you're playing with M20 rules for spheres, it might be simpler to just keep like with like.<br /> There's a table for that somewhere in M20, though details won't be around until Book of Secrets comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T19:31:56-08:00","id":1011313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1011304#post1011304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok - First of all Thank YOU :-) <br /> <br /> Now - I got the combat ( 10 pages ) and casting magick ( 10 pages ) printed out, will throw out those that seem overkill later on. <br /> <br /> Also, Holy crap! I expected Umbra to be complicated but this is just crazy. I will stick to mage 20th info and your link guide to galaxy as that's exactly what I was looking for - a quick look at how this is built. <br /> <br /> your questions- <br /> <br /> 1) Yes, I want the avatar storm - mainly as a form of delay before the spirit guy hacks his way through the gauntlet. <br /> <br /> 2) Spirit guy is a Verbena modern shaman ( ER doctor in his mundane life ) with strong life ( 3) and spirit ( 3 ) and basic prime ( 1 ) . He has celtic/irish roots and that's his paradigm as well - a modern druid so to speak. He is curious about the spirit world but wants to take thing slow about it. <br /> <br /> 3) My chronicle is based in NY - It will be focused in this city at least for few months before they choose to do something else. <br /> <br /> 4) I haven't used spirits yet, but I want to yes - I wanted to introduce the city father and the chronicle will touch the egiptian spirits ( They're trying to steal/obtain an ancient egiptian artifact ). <br /> <br /> 5) Not for the time being as I'm not confident about Umbra at all - if anything your post freaked me out even more haha<br /> <br /> 6) Doubt they would want to do that - but hey - if they do I would rather be prepared.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, sorry about that. The umbra is one of the ways White Wolf managed to have all their game lines exist in the same universe, so to know it in it's entirety is to be familiar with four different systems. Intimidating? Yes! But necessary? Not quite.<br /> <br /> The best place to start is with the Book of Worlds. It's the friendliest book of the bunch for Mage players and assumes no prior exposure with the Umbra.<br /> <br /> First thing to figure out is how he'll see the penumbra. This is known as the Videre, and it's described well in Book of Worlds.<br /> <br /> As a Verbena, he'll probably be more interested in exploring the Spirit Wilds, and Book of Worlds should have you covered or this. Only read through WTA's umbra books if you're left wanting more.<br /> <br /> Don't forget though, that the umbra is constantly changing in ways both subtle and overt. So nothing says you can't creat realms within it which ad hear to your own rules. Want to make a realm where everything is made of Candy? Go for it! Want to make one where everyone's a vampire? By all means. The umbra is yours to play with.<br /> <br /> By the way, if it helps, my current chronicle has a pair of Mages questing in the Umbra, so you can have a read of that if you'd like an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-02-2016, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T05:31:50-08:00","id":1013698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1011304#post1011304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Yes, I want the avatar storm - mainly as a form of delay before the spirit guy hacks his way through the gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Spirit guy will just have a hard time going there, he can still use his Spirit to consult spirits, ask for favours and get them to do things for him. Paradox free even!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1011304#post1011304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) I haven't used spirits yet, but I want to yes - I wanted to introduce the city father and the chronicle will touch the egiptian spirits ( They're trying to steal/obtain an ancient egiptian artifact ).<br /> <br /> 5) Not for the time being as I'm not confident about Umbra at all - if anything your post freaked me out even more haha</div> </div> </div> </div>That list of books is intimidating, but Umbra isn't at all. It's just an excuse to toss anything you wish into the game. Spirits are representations of ideas, events and things of our world (and possibly some other worlds). The places they live in are shaped by what they are about. Yes, among those you can find all possible mythological beings and religious pantheons - so any idea you have will work.<br /> <br /> There are two basic layers of the Umbra<br /> - one which is just an eerie echo and shadow of our world where night is day and where all sorts of things have spirits that go about their business and seek to improve their power through advancing their poofolio<br /> - the other which are the myriad realms and far away places which include mythical places like Avalon, Shangri la, Valhalla and the Land of the Lost or maybe crazy afterlives, godly palaces, fractal planes of mathematics, living representations of planets and Cradles of Life. They can even include past events, future events or even whole alternate realities...<br /> <br /> The nuances are so varied and with odd interactions that you should focus on what suits you and not worry too much about what books have to say about it. Just see what inspires you and what you might like to use. For instance, how about a group in your New York that follows and praises the Egyptian Gods? As they do, their reverence and rites give power to the Gods (highly powerful spirits) which first reshape the local Umbra into a semblance of their own vision of how a land should look before they start possesing people and bringing their power into the mortal realm...<br /> <br /> Or maybe there is a chantry into which an ancient egyptian artifact was brought and since it has been brought there, the Chantry has a gateway into a mythical Ancient Egypt where Gods do as they will? Or maybe the long forgotten Geb lives his life as a limping hobo that occasionaly performs strange wonders and dreams of being reunited with Nut, who may or may not actually live in New York...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T13:43:03-08:00","id":1015356,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys - much appriciated :-)<br /> <br /> It's been three games so far and for the first time in years, players are crazy obsessed about this game :-) We're talking adults between 30-35 years, discussing the past games on fb for hours, creating extended history of their characters and all that. It's amazing. <br /> <br /> Now, question of the day! The Euthanatoi girl began studying mistic martial arts ( my games are a poor mans copy of Tarantinos style, kitsch and lots of pop culture ) - so the question is, what spheres would require the famous .... <b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NL7nLSSSWjw\" target=\"_blank\">The Five Point Palm Exploding Heart Technique</a>'</b><br /><br /> :-D<br /> I already plan to make a narrative event for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T15:20:59-08:00","id":1015379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1015356#post1015356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks guys - much appriciated :-)<br /> <br /> It's been three games so far and for the first time in years, players are crazy obsessed about this game :-) We're talking adults between 30-35 years, discussing the past games on fb for hours, creating extended history of their characters and all that. It's amazing. <br /> <br /> Now, question of the day! The Euthanatoi girl began studying mistic martial arts ( my games are a poor mans copy of Tarantinos style, kitsch and lots of pop culture ) - so the question is, what spheres would require the famous .... <b><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NL7nLSSSWjw&amp;quot;]The</a> Five Point Palm Exploding Heart Technique[/URL]'</b><br /><br /> :-D<br /> I already plan to make a narrative event for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time 4 to deliver a damaging effect(Life 3 or Entropy 4 or ...) later","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T16:21:44-08:00","id":1015403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1015379#post1015379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Time 4 to deliver a damaging effect(Life 3 or Entropy 4 or ...) later</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You wouldn't necessarily need Time 4. You could just put duration into the effect and have the damage slowly doled out over the length of a Scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:43:08-08:00","id":1017035,"title":"","content":"Hi guys - fourth game and yet another blast of a game :-)<br /> <br /> This time due to some freak incident my group got their hands on a rather ancient Vampire artefact that they decided to sell to the Tremere in exchange for future favours AND information on a potential node. I was wondering where would any of you GM's go with ideas when it comes to this deal. Would the Tremere hand over a potential place of power and if so would there be a trick ? ( It's never so simple with the Tremere is it? ) . The artifact in question was indeed very valuable, holding some hints of a location that could have been an shelter of an ancient. ( I left it vague as I felt they wouldn't pursue but guess what *sigh* ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12551,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","user":"artuard","date":".  typo 12-14-2016, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:10:43-08:00","id":1017160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1017035#post1017035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys - fourth game and yet another blast of a game :-)<br /> <br /> This time due to some freak incident my group got their hands on a rather ancient Vampire artefact that they decided to sell to the Tremere in exchange for future favours AND information on a potential node. I was wondering where would any of you GM's go with ideas when it comes to this deal. Would the Tremere hand over a potential place of power and if so would there be a trick ? ( It's never so simple with the Tremere is it? ) . The artifact in question was indeed very valuable, holding some hints of a location that could have been an shelter of an ancient. ( I left it vague as I felt they wouldn't pursue but guess what *sigh* ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah never throw out a hint or red herring you do not want the players to follow, because its super awkward when they do. Players have a knack for latching on to such things.<br /> <br /> As for dealing with vampires you will have to determine how crossover rules are going to work. There are a few different options available, but none of them are perfect. M20, Vampire Storyteller's Handbook, Blood Treachery all have different interpretations how to deal with the two groups together. All of them will require some work from you to make decisions and rules calls. Be prepared with as least some basic stuff such as how Disciplines and Spheres interact (things like can a Mage countermagic a Discipline, what kind of countermagic do the vampires have), what happens when a Mage is ghouled/embraced (trust me dont underestimate your player's abilities to make strange decisions and actions).<br /> <br /> You also need to figure out if you want this to be a limited contact or a plot hook that will pop up repeatedly.<br /> <br /> (Warning Metaplot used ahead)<br /> As for the Tremere it depends on a few factors. The first is whether the events of the Second Massassa War have taken place, if so then relations between Tremere and Mages are at an all time low constantly simmering just outside of war again. This would likely preclude anything other than betrayal from the Tremere since working with Mages could be seen as an act of treason from either side's leadership should they find out. <br /> <br /> The exception would be the value of this artefact. In Transylvania Chronicles and Nights of Prophecy it is revealed Saulot has succeeded in taking over Tremere's body and Tremere had to flee into Goratrix's (again based on the metaplot in your game whether or not these occurred). This would mean he is currently limited to the capabilities of a 4th Generation vampire which is not how one wins the Jyhad. Perhaps Tremere has been influencing his clan to seek out information on sleeping ancients again so that he might divine the location of another antediluvian to reclaim his former glory. It would not be so open or foolish as to reveal what had occurred to Tremere merely an agenda added to the docket (left vague so that the regents can read into it what they want, &quot;Seek an ancient, perhaps another will be promoted to the council and they wish blood to go with the station&quot; - for example.<br /> <br /> Depending on how the Tremere view this artefact will determine whether the node offer is good or bad.<br /> <br /> If those events have not occurred then it is somewhat simpler as the conflict between the Tremere and Mages has been slowly cooling for centuries. This makes the dealings on the Tremere side probably made in better faith and with somewhat less backstabbing hoping to gain some useful if young pawns.<br /> <br /> Regardless why would the Tremere offer up a place of power? A few things come to mind.<ul><li>They dont own it, they just know it. In this case the node is claimed by another supernatural group and so it is not immediately useful to the group. This will come off like a betrayal.</li> <li>It has some ongoing negative effect. It could be the node is tainted, haunted, or some other bad thing. The Tremere will be quick to point out that Mages such as themselves should have no problem dealing with whats there. It puts the node in hands the Tremere can monitor. Less betrayal, but still comes off like buying a lemon car.</li> <li>The node is dormant. All the signs are there but the node is not active. The group will have to look into how to reawaken it. This could be anything from rousing a sleeping guardian spirit to performing a certain ritual.</li> <li>A safe secure node seems far too good a prize for such a simple artefact and the Tremere might tell them of it but say they the price for using and holding it will require more from the group. Basically a proper no problem node should have strings attached.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Some things to be aware of.<ul><li>Your players might get it into their head to become ghouled or embraced, be ready for that or how to deal with it or telling them no.</li> <li>Do you want the players to deal with the Tremere again or not? This will affect the quality of their offer.</li> <li>Fire, Forces 2 and a flame available (even as simple as a lighter) will allow the Mage to hurt gouts of Rotschreck inducing aggravated damage causing fire at the vampires. Mages are super dangerous to vampires for this reason.</li> <li>Dominate, Without Mind dealing with Dominated characters can be very difficult and can lead to a disempowered feeling from the players as the vampire gets to command their character like a meat puppet.</li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T15:55:44-08:00","id":1017366,"title":"","content":"There's a point the above post is neglecting: how do the Tremere know the site in question is a Node? How would they even know what a Node was? Sure, Methuselahs who were originally Mages back in the day would know about Crays, but would a modern Tremere who never was a Mage or had any ties to the Order of Hermes know anything about that? Is it at all likely that a Tremere old enough to remember that would be the ones dealing with a random group of Mages? (In that last case, I have the answer: No, it isn't. Any Tremere that old doesn't have the time to spare dealing with this business. They'll have a younger Clan member deal with this business on their behalf, assuming they know about the deal at all).<br /> <br /> So...does Clan Tremere even know what it's offering? They can't see Quintessence flows, even with Auspex.<br /> <br /> I suppose the Node would be creating Tass on the regular - Tass typically makes up half of any given Node's output. The Tremere could be aware that the site produces said Tass, which could be used as a Ritual component for Thaumaturgy. It may be that the kind of Tass the Node produces doesn't have a Resonance that works well with most Tremere Rituals (blood magic tends to be darker and more twisted than mortal equivalents, requiring ingredients of similar quality). As such, they couldn't get much value from the site...but they know enough about mortal magic to know that the Tass can be of greater value to the Mages. The deal being made is basically the Clan attempting to trade a sub-optimal resource for an artifact they treasure more highly, to a group that doesn't understand the artifact's worth but would gain much greater value from the site.<br /> <br /> All things considered, a good trade for both parties. The Tremere don't really need to double-cross the Cabal, unless they seriously think the Cabal will betray them first.<br /> <br /> I suggest having the deal go off as quickly as possible, with the Tremere exiting stage left as quickly as possible. Given how much vampires love their privacy, this is entirely in character, and not just a way to avoid sidetracking the plot. Further, when the PCs get their hands on the Node site, it could see altogether hunky dory...for the time being. Any number of complications could come to light after the characters have held it for a while. Just long enough to figure out a good story hook from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T00:18:55-08:00","id":1017524,"title":"","content":"Loving all the answers so far! This helps a great deal guys. SO I will roll with the following : <br /> <br /> 1) One player will get a discreet proposition of embrace ( not right away, but she is a member of <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Euthanatoi\" target=\"_blank\">Euthanatoi</a>, and I know she would be tempted ;-)<br /> <br /> 2) They will get a node but one that is occupied by some other supernaturals. <br /> <br /> 3) Tremere will often require service and will be happy to provide service. So I assume a deal will be struck and would be mutually beneficial ( so to speak ). <br /> <br /> I don't want to embrace them all or kill them right away although that does seem plausible with how they approached Tremere, but they seem more useful as pawns that could be used than dead?<br /> <br /> I figured you could use more info: Mages in question are one Hermetic, one Verbena and one Euthanatoi girl. <br /> The item is a cross of true faith that was used to banish evil - twist is that it has a vial of blood of an ancient that had that true faith.( or has, I left that open if he's dead or not ) Tremere know that. <br /> Does that sound too far fetched?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T21:38:51-08:00","id":1017947,"title":"","content":"Well first, why would the Tremere offer the Embrace to the Euthanatos instead of the Hermetic? Sure, Death Mages would be appropriate for vampirism - at least from a surface perspective (the Euthanatoi as a culture have a low opinion of the undead) - but the Hermetic would take to the Tremere's form of blood sorcery more easily than the Euthanatos.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, why would the Tremere offer the Embrace to Mages at all? The Clan would need to see something worth having in the character. I'm not saying you can't go this route, but I am saying that Clan Tremere doesn't embrace just anyone. They have standards and needs.<br /> <br /> Plus, Mages that are Embraced lose their prior magical ability, and need to start from the beginning again, because blood sorcery is sufficiently different from Awakened magick or even unAwakened Sorcery. They'd only retain their understanding of metaphysical theory (Occult, Esoterica, etc.), and the Tremere could get that from any mundane occultist. And a mundane occultist wouldn't know intimately what they've lost, or have dangerous ties to Mage society. Often enough, a former Mage is more trouble than she's worth.<br /> <br /> Again, this doesn't preclude the embrace happening. It just means that the Clan needs to have a damn good reason for wanting the character brought into their ranks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T21:43:36-08:00","id":1017949,"title":"","content":"Second, if the artifact contains blood from a vampire that is now a Methuselah, that is all the reason a Tremere would need to want it for themselves. It provides a sympathetic link to the vampire in question, which can be used to find (and magically target) them wherever they are. So wanting the artifact makes perfect sense for them...assuming they have members who aren't repelled by the True Faith permeating the object. That could be a hitch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T04:13:51-08:00","id":1018414,"title":"","content":"Valid points Bluecho. Out last game however has moved the plot forward without the embrace being brought up. I was worried for a while that the undead theme would take over my mage game but...then the paradox hit and we're back in the magick joyride haha. They're currently in Iraq ( I ruled a backlash based on 2 botches of correspondence roll would throw them as far as possible to some dangerous place, with their car, in the middle of the desert. ). So, they still desire that node but at the moment they have different things on their mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T16:34:56-08:00","id":1028749,"title":"","content":"Hi there,<br /> <br /> So our games took our group to some crazy places. Most recently to Baghdad, where my misfits managed to accidentally kill a friendly Ah Il Batim mage. Freak accident while using an artifact ( plot related ). With his demise, I figured in a twisted way I could give them access to a hidden node - one that could be visited by using an artifact that the fallen friend had. I was thinking it's a key that could be put into any classic door with a lock, and unlock a passage to the said node/sanctum. They're on a run for at least 6 games now with little to zero downtime and respite. My question so: does it even sound plausible in this game? A magical key that can be used on most doors to bet to a pocket in umbra maybe ( or actual corr effect to teleport to a real life location )? Would it be too easy? Or OP?<br /> <br /> I have yet to think exactly what I want to give them this way, a node, maybe a small library and a sanctum : a base of operations. I really feel like they deserve something even if they got it by ' freak accident'. Not sure how the aforementioned place would look like - open to ideas !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12551,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","user":"artuard","date":". 01-08-2017, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:03:10-08:00","id":1028769,"title":"","content":"Plausible? This is Mage. Anything is plausible, so long as there's an internal logic to it.<br /> <br /> And, really, a key like that can easily be seen as a Talisman, with an attached Correspondence 4 effect for opening a portal to a specific location, and maybe a Matter 3 effect to let the key fit any lock. It's hardly all that impressive in the long run, when any Mage who hits Arete 4 and Correspondence 4 can do the same thing on their own.<br /> <br /> I've said this before on the forum, but many of us gamers become hyper-sensitive to things that could remotely be called &quot;Overpowered&quot;. In a tabletop RPG, though, the players already have the freedom to do anything they can imagine (and the Storyteller allows). They could make one or two dots in Resources overpowered, if they are clever enough. Something that seems dramatic and game-breaking on paper might appear far less so when taken in the context of the larger world the characters inhabit.<br /> <br /> For one, the key is a key. Keys can be stolen or misplaced. If they lose the key, they don't just lose access to the Node, but all the crap they stored in the location. If they more or less &quot;moved in&quot; to the Sanctum, they might lose a lot of valuable stuff there (especially if the physical location is difficult or impossible to get to otherwise). For another, this key requires a door with a lock in it to function. No doors, no access. A big deal if the characters are stranded in the middle of the wilderness.<br /> <br /> If the group is separated, only the individual(s) with the key on them can effect a quick escape. This necessitates a greater degree of coordination among the cabal, as some or most could be left without an easy trip &quot;home&quot; if the group scatters.<br /> <br /> On another note, the key was pillaged off the corpse of a Batini. It stands to reason, then, that the Sanctum they gained access to is &quot;formatted&quot; to that Batini's Paradigm. Ergo, Ahl-I-Batin magick is Coincidental there, while all other magicks are Vulgar. This can create a whole host of headaches for the cabal, if they think they can get away with anything in their new crib. Make the process of &quot;deprogramming&quot; the space as long, arduous, and time-consuming as you want. Sancta aren't easy to create, let alone convert to one's personal use.<br /> <br /> Finally, while we're on the subject of Paradox, remember that opening a random door to a different physical location entirely is Vulgar, in most places in the world. The Ahl-I-Batin are masters of subtlety and stealth, so they would know how to mask the transition and avoid the Paradox. Does the player cabal know how? Probably not. If they've been using it a fair bit so far, start keeping a tally of the number of times, with a steadily increasing pool of Paradox points stored on the key. It's a Talisman, so it could store Paradox without the user knowing. Once it fills up with as much 'Dox as it has Quintessence storage space, roll a backlash and have it apply to the user.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:34:10-08:00","id":1028792,"title":"","content":"Don't worry whether something is &quot;over powered&quot; or not. As Bluecho says, OP stuff is par the course in a Mage game, and starts to fall apart if examined.<br /> <br /> Instead, just pay close attention to whether they players rely on a certain item of technique a little too often. Then adapt the game slightly to see how they deal when said item or technique starts giving them trouble.<br /> <br /> For example, if you think they are beginning to use this key too much, see what happens when a rival mage starts to fight them for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T19:48:53-08:00","id":1028843,"title":"","content":"Thanks Guys.<br /> Now that you put it that way, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> it really looks better. I was thinking about giving them library and node access via that key. The Sanctum would be somewhere in Umbra ( non of them have spirit or will have for a while ), so it will make sense for them to watch that key closely. I'm thinking, node 2, library 3 ( requires Arabic for most of the books or some form of magic to understand the language. ) and some bits and pieces that add to the flavour of the place ( a caged Djinn with one wish left ). I forgot one has to reformat the paradigm of the place to fully use it to cast coincidental magic. I must say I lack knowledge of the Batim so i will have to explore more about their paradigms. Also how does one exactly reprogram the paradigm of the place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T21:05:46-08:00","id":1028856,"title":"","content":"Undoing the original owner's work to make a space into a Sanctum is a matter of roleplaying, less about mechanics. They're going to be consecrating the Sanctum to their own Paradigms, which can be a long and intricate process, informed by those same Paradigms. As such, it will be highly dependent on their Focus.<br /> <br /> As a start, ask the players, from the characters' perspectives, how they would go about making the space <i>theirs</i>. A Chorister might go from room to room, splashing holy water and loudly praying for God's blessing. A Hermetic might draw complicated warding sigils on the floors, walls, and around doors and windows. A Virtual Adept might work to remove every hint of dust (particles that small wreak havoc on electronics), and lay out extensive electrical wires and nerdy posters. More or less, you're trying to cast an Effect without actually casting an Effect, and as much thought should go into creating a Sanctum as one would cast a spell.<br /> <br /> Just, you know, taking much longer. M20 doesn't specify how long it takes to make a Sanctum, but earlier editions had it somewhere in the ballpark of 5 years per dot in the Sanctum background. Feel free to not go quite that far, if it doesn't serve the game. Still, carving out a place in the Consensus where one's personal magick reigns supreme should not be a quick task. It takes commitment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:04:32-08:00","id":1029029,"title":"","content":"Sounds good man, appreciate :-) Chances are they will not even look for the key on the body. They're really on a run and behave like animals. I might have pushed the open world a bit hard on them. They opened many cans of worms, tried many different things but hardly focused long enough to explore something to the end.<br /> <br /> But it's good to be prepared for an option..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:40:35-08:00","id":1029053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1029029#post1029029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They opened many cans of worms, tried many different things but hardly focused long enough to explore something to the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a standard troupe of players if you ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T09:38:35-08:00","id":1029123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1029053#post1029053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a standard troupe of players if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for completely random and unimportant things that catch their attention...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:21:11-08:00","id":1029140,"title":"","content":"Agreed - they're not really any different from most groups I guess. The only long term issue I have with this that after our 8th game I start to feel creative exhaustion if that makes sense. Our games are a roller coaster of ideas that they feed me and I elaborate on that creating stories, side events etc. But I am tired <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For once I would like to finish one idea - because I've put some thought in those from the start and I feel a bit drained. That's worrying for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:51:46-08:00","id":1029156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>artuard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1029140#post1029140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed - they're not really any different from most groups I guess. The only long term issue I have with this that after our 8th game I start to feel creative exhaustion if that makes sense. Our games are a roller coaster of ideas that they feed me and I elaborate on that creating stories, side events etc. But I am tired <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For once I would like to finish one idea - because I've put some thought in those from the start and I feel a bit drained. That's worrying for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's understandable. Nothing says you can't force the matter if you think they're running away from the plot.<br /> Make one of the people they are being chased by happen to come across them on the road or something. Force a confrontation, and make it clear with the events in place that if they don't start resolving things by themselves, that the NPCs will happily resolve it for them, and not in a way they'd like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T01:53:19-08:00","id":1029506,"title":"","content":"Also - my main plot was related to an item that will eventually after much adventures and research lead my mage group to some mysterious arch nemesis BUT! Once they reach that creature I wanted to switch systems to Vampire DA where the new group of Vamps would be somehow responsible either for the 'containment' of said being or linked in some other direct way. <br /> <br /> Suffice to say they're more interested in how clubbing and random teleportations ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T06:11:24-08:00","id":1031549,"title":"","content":"Hi guys, newby GM here :-)<br /> <br /> So my game goes on fine - but my pc's have reached a stage in game where they want to increase spheres/arete. I've granted them the Library background ( all in arabic but that's besides the point ) and ruled that all spheres could be learnt from this source however it's Batim paradigm related ( as discussed in previous posts above). Any idea how should I rule this? As in how do they increase spheres with a foreign library even if they know the language ( we're talking level 2 spheres or new spheres ) - time wise/xp/narrative?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12551-artuard","name":"artuard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12551_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:10:00-08:00","id":1031640,"title":"","content":"I generally rule that my players can level up any spheres they already have with Experience. The assumption being that simply using their spheres should be enough to gain the familiarity and practice necessary to increase in understanding them. They are one of the most expensive stats after all.<br /> <br /> To learn new spheres, however, requires a lot more time. If done by one's own self I rule it would take several months at best before they'd develop understanding of a completely foreign sphere. However, this time can be greatly shortened if they have access to material which fits in with their paradigm, and shortened ever still if there is a suitable mentor with the spheres desired.<br /> <br /> So if it would take 5-6 months to learn a new sphere with nothing but your own wits. I'd say starting with a good deal of useful information, say a library of relevant information, should reduce this to 2-3 months, and a mentor may bring this down to 2-3 weeks.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, in my games learning new spheres is almost exclusively a Downtime activity.<br /> <br /> If all they have access to is a library filled with material which is completely outside of their belief system, it simply would not be of any use to them. However, I might rule that they could spend a week or two rolling to translate the information across paradigms. This would only work if there are overlaps in the belief. For example, a Dreamspeaker may be able to translate aspects of a Verbena's Book of Shadows into their own paradigm in order to further their understanding in a new sphere. However, this would depend on whether this particular Dreamspeakers paradigm happened to overlap with the words of this particular Book of Shadows.<br /> <br /> As another example, if a Virtual Adept who deals in numeric code came across a Hermetic Tome of Natural Neumerology, they may be able to gleam something from it with a few weeks worth of rolling Intelligence + Enigmas.<br /> <br /> As a final note, not all mages learn well from books. Perhaps an Etherite gets more out of building and experimenting, or an Ecstatic requires experiencing the sphere first hand, or a Dreamspeaker can only learn through travel. In each case, having a library would be of little consolation to these mages. Interesting stuff certainly, but not particularly enlightening.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding Arete, I treat it similarly to gaining a new level in an old sphere with one crucial difference. You buy it with Exp, but you're not actually buying the next rank of Arete, instead you buy the right to have attempt a Seeking. and that will only happen when the Avatar is good and ready to provide one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-14-2017, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T16:36:39-08:00","id":1031879,"title":"","content":"Like Saikou above, I would say that trying to learn from Batini material is going to be harder if none of the characters are Batini, as opposed to them learning from members of their own Traditions. If anything, trying to translate knowledge from the Ahl-I-Batin Paradigm to their own may do more harm than good, as it confuses the issue.<br /> <br /> That said, certain Traditions have an easier time gaining knowledge from the Batini than others. Hermetics, Solificati, and Choristers all come from cultures that have been influenced by Middle Eastern mysticism, or else were the ones who influenced Middle Eastern mysticism. Alchemy from the West was preserved and iterated upon in Persia and Arabia, as many of the texts of the subject made their way there. The same is true of some High Ritual Magick, which drew elements from Zoroastrian, Sumerian, Babylonian, and other cultural practices. Abrahamic beliefs, like Christian and Islamic mysticism and Kabbala, had their starts in the same region, so many of those fed into the Hermetics, Choristers, and Batini.<br /> <br /> So if any characters are of those groups, they might be able to make use of the texts in the Batini library. Assuming they can translate the material faithfully (a poor translation could result in important ideas not being conveyed properly; there's a reason Hermetics often learn multiple languages).<br /> <br /> If they can't make use of the material directly to enrich their understanding, it isn't completely useless. Those texts are invaluable tomes of lore and arcana. Any one of them could fetch a high price with other Mages. It would probably behoove the Cabal to make copies of relevant books, as they can trade them to other Traditionalists for copies of books more immediately useful for the cabal. The cabal can keep the original books for themselves, while still leveraging the knowledge as a resource. And given that these are books from an Ahl-I-Batin library - one of the most enigmatic and secretive Crafts - they will be especially in demand.<br /> <br /> Provided, of course, the player characters can figure out what each book actually contains. So doing a bit of translation is still in order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T17:22:48-08:00","id":1031893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/988329-new-gm-needs-some-help?p=1031879#post1031879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Provided, of course, the player characters can figure out what each book actually contains. So doing a bit of translation is still in order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine if they spend all this time considering the possibilities of learning and selling, start making promises to bidders, and get ready to translate the paradigm, when it turns out all these books are just a collection of Arabian Nights styled fanfictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}